1
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:08,780
No living creatures were harmed
during the filming.

2
00:02:09,610 --> 00:02:14,280
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:16,480
I told you that I would come for you.

4
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:20,380
You are in my hand now.

5
00:02:20,820 --> 00:02:24,660
You wanted to keep the beys
away from me.

6
00:02:25,630 --> 00:02:29,700
Who is he to do that, Osman Bey?

7
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:34,240
So, you are the most capable
commander, huh?

8
00:02:37,410 --> 00:02:39,740
Capable. Very capable!

9
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:42,980
That's why he depends on
the rogues.

10
00:02:43,040 --> 00:02:45,870
I'll work with the devil even.
Just to destroy the Turks.

11
00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:49,700
Don't worry.

12
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:02,800
I know that you want to take
Nikea and Bursa.

13
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:05,420
You know it surely.

14
00:03:06,510 --> 00:03:09,860
But you know that I won't stop too.

15
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:15,650
Now, you'll tell me the name
of the traitor.

16
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:25,650
I never liked Nikola.

17
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:29,010
But we are made of the same material.

18
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:33,520
Take my head but it won't
make me speak.

19
00:03:34,670 --> 00:03:38,790
Atabey Ahmet. You worked with him.

20
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:41,230
He was with you.

21
00:03:42,020 --> 00:03:43,230
Let's say, he was.

22
00:03:44,540 --> 00:03:45,980
How will you prove it?

23
00:03:49,620 --> 00:03:51,280
I'm not in a hurry.

24
00:03:52,740 --> 00:03:54,830
Your plots will be revealed.

25
00:03:55,260 --> 00:03:56,830
And so will the traitor.

26
00:03:58,420 --> 00:04:00,770
And you'll lose your head.

27
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:12,010
But you'll beg me to kill you
sooner then.

28
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:26,350
Now, tell me the traitor in the tribe...

29
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:28,580
and receive a swift death.

30
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:50,850
Selvi...
It's because of me...

31
00:05:00,130 --> 00:05:02,000
I couldn't protect you.

32
00:05:05,540 --> 00:05:07,010
I couldn't.

33
00:05:14,610 --> 00:05:17,040
But I promise you that...

34
00:05:17,730 --> 00:05:19,380
my enduring wife...

35
00:05:21,650 --> 00:05:23,730
the one who took your life...

36
00:05:25,310 --> 00:05:30,490
and the one who was involved
will have no corner to hide.

37
00:05:31,870 --> 00:05:33,710
Firstly, that dog Cebe...

38
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:36,770
then Osman...

39
00:05:39,550 --> 00:05:42,190
I'll kill them all.

40
00:05:44,930 --> 00:05:47,020
I promise you, Selvi.

41
00:05:50,940 --> 00:05:52,540
I promise you.

42
00:06:18,590 --> 00:06:20,480
My condolences, Barkın Bey.

43
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:23,630
Thank you.

44
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:30,550
Women.

45
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:33,940
I was rude.

46
00:06:34,940 --> 00:06:36,150
Forgive me.

47
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:38,770
It's my pain.

48
00:06:40,340 --> 00:06:43,440
Otherwise, I know what you
did for Selvi.

49
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:46,160
Give me your blessing.

50
00:06:48,750 --> 00:06:50,480
It's yours, Barkın Bey.

51
00:06:53,440 --> 00:06:54,820
It happens.

52
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:57,630
Our pain is fresh.

53
00:07:01,650 --> 00:07:03,380
Our pain is common.

54
00:07:05,380 --> 00:07:06,590
It's yours.

55
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:09,730
We did all we could but...

56
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:12,010
we couldn't make it in time.

57
00:07:13,970 --> 00:07:16,130
You have my blessing, Barkın Bey.

58
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:31,150
My Selvi...

59
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:34,940
My beautiful sister.

60
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:39,410
Forgive me, sister.

61
00:07:43,650 --> 00:07:45,740
I couldn't protect you.

62
00:08:00,940 --> 00:08:02,270
Selvi...

63
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:31,470
Not being afraid of death is
valiant to a point...

64
00:08:32,609 --> 00:08:33,770
now...

65
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:38,609
let's see if you'll endure
this pain.

66
00:08:40,140 --> 00:08:43,630
Is your endurance enough
for a lit sword.

67
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:51,100
It's your endurance that
will be tested today, Osman Bey!

68
00:08:58,640 --> 00:09:00,080
Let's talk!

69
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:02,210
I'm a wolf in the den of a jackal!

70
00:09:04,610 --> 00:09:05,900
Warriors!

71
00:09:15,860 --> 00:09:16,940
We are here, my bey!

72
00:09:17,540 --> 00:09:19,980
Setting an ambush over an ambush?

73
00:09:20,780 --> 00:09:24,050
You need to be smarter to set
a trap here.

74
00:09:37,310 --> 00:09:38,940
This one is the last, my bey.

75
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:40,940
There are no more scouts.

76
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:42,740
Thank you.

77
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:46,400
Now, get all the swords
and bows.

78
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:48,400
Leave nothing.

79
00:09:49,630 --> 00:09:51,360
Şamil. Turalp.

80
00:09:52,430 --> 00:09:54,320
You'll infiltrate from
the left flank.

81
00:09:54,500 --> 00:09:55,580
Don't make a mistake.

82
00:09:56,180 --> 00:09:57,580
We play an important part.

83
00:09:57,940 --> 00:09:58,990
Yes, my bey.

84
00:09:59,090 --> 00:10:00,450
Yes, my bey.

85
00:10:00,670 --> 00:10:04,780
Alps, we'll infiltrate from the
right flank.

86
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:09,860
With Osman Bey's plan, this is the
last day of the tyrants.

87
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:11,210
Come on, put them on.

88
00:10:11,210 --> 00:10:12,700
Yes, my bey.

89
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:45,600
He traces well!

90
00:10:46,180 --> 00:10:49,090
You can't even see what's in front of
your eyes, Cebe!

91
00:10:49,090 --> 00:10:53,200
I'll rip you into so many pieces that
no one will find you.

92
00:11:07,230 --> 00:11:09,710
You won't die before killing Osman!
Get up!

93
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:19,070
My bey!
I'll go after him!

94
00:11:33,340 --> 00:11:36,030
Traitor!
The disgrace of the Mongols!

95
00:11:36,350 --> 00:11:38,450
Many called me a traitor.

96
00:11:38,850 --> 00:11:41,790
Now they are all dead.

97
00:11:54,400 --> 00:11:55,700
Are you hitting a man...

98
00:11:56,100 --> 00:11:57,540
or are you forging a weapon?

99
00:11:57,810 --> 00:11:59,760
You are not bad either, Şamil!

100
00:12:07,870 --> 00:12:10,540
Brother, I watch your back!

101
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:16,080
Me too, brother!

102
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:55,420
Osman.

103
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:57,840
Osman, yes.

104
00:13:04,740 --> 00:13:07,200
He ran away from a stone to hit
a rock.

105
00:13:23,580 --> 00:13:26,510
If anyone follows us,
kill them all!

106
00:13:43,340 --> 00:13:44,880
Romanos!

107
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:47,680
I will kill you!

108
00:13:48,340 --> 00:13:49,680
You can't run away!

109
00:13:50,430 --> 00:13:52,050
Heathens!

110
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:56,530
I'll kill you first and your
commander later.

111
00:14:24,100 --> 00:14:25,490
We are here, my valiant!

112
00:14:25,490 --> 00:14:26,640
Allah is righteous!

113
00:14:55,090 --> 00:14:57,900
I won't die before seeing
them dead.

114
00:14:58,130 --> 00:15:00,050
I lost whoever I served.

115
00:15:00,750 --> 00:15:04,340
But Rome always takes revenge,
Commander Romanos.

116
00:15:04,340 --> 00:15:05,430
Yes.

117
00:15:05,900 --> 00:15:09,460
But for that, we need to survive first.

118
00:15:37,410 --> 00:15:39,980
So, this is why you
served Romanos.

119
00:15:40,260 --> 00:15:42,670
Yes. Don't you think it's enough?

120
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:49,940
I had to, to survive.

121
00:15:50,720 --> 00:15:52,260
We lost everything.

122
00:15:53,390 --> 00:15:55,390
If you want to survive.

123
00:15:56,700 --> 00:15:59,220
Then, you'll tell me everything
you know.

124
00:16:00,980 --> 00:16:06,570
And surely, if surviving is
that much important to you.

125
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:09,600
I'll do anything to live.

126
00:16:10,820 --> 00:16:11,780
Now...

127
00:16:13,780 --> 00:16:17,580
tell me the traitor sending news
to Romanos from our tribe.

128
00:16:18,850 --> 00:16:21,090
I can't say that because they
didn't tell me.

129
00:16:22,180 --> 00:16:23,680
I don't know, Osman Bey.

130
00:16:31,380 --> 00:16:33,390
They never trusted me, Osman Bey!

131
00:16:33,680 --> 00:16:35,120
They didn't say it!

132
00:16:35,250 --> 00:16:36,480
I beg you!
Spare my life!

133
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:38,380
I beg you!
Let me live!

134
00:16:38,380 --> 00:16:39,330
Let me be your dog.

135
00:16:39,500 --> 00:16:41,330
If I'm a dog, let me serve you!

136
00:16:41,580 --> 00:16:44,020
I beg you, Osman Bey! Let me live!
I beg you!

137
00:16:50,430 --> 00:16:52,800
Let me live, I beg you!

138
00:17:13,740 --> 00:17:16,880
İnegöl Castle

139
00:17:29,490 --> 00:17:30,770
You are better.

140
00:17:31,170 --> 00:17:32,770
You are a murderer!

141
00:17:33,380 --> 00:17:34,770
You killed my atabey!

142
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:51,120
Stop, shehzad.

143
00:17:51,310 --> 00:17:53,130
You are mad, I know.

144
00:17:53,230 --> 00:17:54,620
You want to destroy.

145
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:57,190
But stop. Stop and listen.

146
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:06,590
You are a murderer!

147
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:09,290
And every word you speak
is a lie!

148
00:18:09,430 --> 00:18:10,910
Why should I listen?

149
00:18:13,640 --> 00:18:16,850
I'll get your head when I'm
saved, Turgut!

150
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:19,690
Mashallah, you are strong.

151
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:22,810
But sometimes stopping is better
than acting.

152
00:18:22,900 --> 00:18:24,810
Otherwise, how will you hear
what I say?

153
00:18:24,930 --> 00:18:27,150
Stop!

154
00:18:35,660 --> 00:18:39,370
You should've seen me when I was young.
I would deflect your strike.

155
00:18:39,620 --> 00:18:41,330
But I'm old now.

156
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:43,330
Come now!

157
00:19:02,670 --> 00:19:04,200
Tie him.

158
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:06,230
His mouth too.

159
00:19:27,910 --> 00:19:30,520
You are deaf to my words.
You don't hear it.

160
00:19:32,120 --> 00:19:34,210
But you have to hear now.

161
00:19:34,700 --> 00:19:37,490
I'll speak the language you
understand, kid.

162
00:19:40,640 --> 00:19:42,710
I pity your father.

163
00:19:43,050 --> 00:19:46,600
I pity him for having a son like
you to leave his beylig.

164
00:19:46,990 --> 00:19:49,390
Someone who can't
hear or see.

165
00:19:49,570 --> 00:19:53,220
You can only destroy! Solid wrath!
What about justice?

166
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:58,910
What will you do when your
wrath isn't enough?

167
00:20:01,230 --> 00:20:03,340
I know it's hard for you, but...

168
00:20:03,520 --> 00:20:08,580
to understand what's going on,
you need silence and wits.

169
00:20:08,780 --> 00:20:10,700
But you don't have it.

170
00:20:14,650 --> 00:20:18,100
I didn't kill your atabey.

171
00:20:19,380 --> 00:20:23,430
Surely, I wanted to rip his traitor
head off.

172
00:20:24,120 --> 00:20:28,220
But we make our moves justly.

173
00:20:33,230 --> 00:20:35,870
This is the real greatness.

174
00:20:39,150 --> 00:20:41,130
We are in a big game, son.

175
00:20:41,330 --> 00:20:45,760
I hope it won't be too late for everything
when you see it.

176
00:20:46,150 --> 00:20:49,430
Thank Allah that your father Ali Bey
will learn the truth.

177
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:52,850
Maybe you'll believe him then.

178
00:21:20,810 --> 00:21:23,420
What are you up to, Barkın Bey?

179
00:21:32,130 --> 00:21:35,840
Bala. You don't look well.

180
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:38,510
There is something off with you.

181
00:21:40,760 --> 00:21:42,290
Selvi is gone, Aygül.

182
00:21:42,470 --> 00:21:45,910
But she left a mistery behind her.

183
00:21:46,120 --> 00:21:48,190
What are you saying, Bala.

184
00:21:50,930 --> 00:21:52,910
She said something...

185
00:21:53,650 --> 00:21:56,800
What did she say?
I hope it's good.

186
00:22:07,940 --> 00:22:10,970
My condolences, Barkın Bey.
May Allah give you patience.

187
00:22:11,150 --> 00:22:14,530
My condolences, Barkın Bey.

188
00:22:41,660 --> 00:22:45,840
Selvi is gone now...

189
00:22:47,260 --> 00:22:48,650
She is gone!

190
00:22:49,550 --> 00:22:51,640
Selvi is gone!

191
00:22:52,880 --> 00:22:57,780
Who will control me now?

192
00:22:58,390 --> 00:22:59,740
Who?

193
00:23:00,300 --> 00:23:02,690
Who will control me now?

194
00:23:16,720 --> 00:23:17,940
My bey.

195
00:23:21,070 --> 00:23:27,210
Even if I burn Kayı Tribe
with its inhabitants...

196
00:23:28,560 --> 00:23:31,190
it won't cool my heart.

197
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:37,400
I couldn't protect my wife.

198
00:23:40,430 --> 00:23:43,180
You couldn't either, Hüsamettin!

199
00:23:44,120 --> 00:23:45,740
My condolences, my bey.

200
00:23:50,920 --> 00:23:52,650
Hüsamettin.

201
00:23:55,140 --> 00:24:03,940
Those who did this and who caused
this will die!

202
00:24:04,480 --> 00:24:09,700
I will kill them all with my
own hands!

203
00:24:18,580 --> 00:24:22,160
Why are you wriggling, Hüsamettin?

204
00:24:23,190 --> 00:24:24,840
Speak.

205
00:24:25,200 --> 00:24:26,910
-My bey.
-Speak!

206
00:24:27,040 --> 00:24:29,900
Osman Bey caught Cebe.

207
00:25:17,720 --> 00:25:19,050
Come!

208
00:25:49,080 --> 00:25:50,790
Welcome, my bey!

209
00:25:57,760 --> 00:25:59,610
Move!

210
00:26:14,560 --> 00:26:18,210
-Cebe! Cebe!
-My bey!

211
00:26:21,310 --> 00:26:25,380
Killing that dog is my job.

212
00:26:25,540 --> 00:26:28,560
I'll skin him alive!

213
00:26:29,030 --> 00:26:32,900
He'll pay for hurting me!

214
00:26:33,190 --> 00:26:35,280
-Let me go!
-My bey!

215
00:26:35,280 --> 00:26:39,350
What if he speaks?

216
00:26:39,470 --> 00:26:41,830
What if he recognizes you?

217
00:26:42,880 --> 00:26:46,480
My bey, if Osman Bey
finds out...

218
00:26:49,120 --> 00:26:52,220
we'll lose our revenge.

219
00:27:30,210 --> 00:27:32,440
Take him to the caged tent.

220
00:27:34,640 --> 00:27:35,800
Move!

221
00:27:37,820 --> 00:27:40,220
Tell me the situation.

222
00:27:40,380 --> 00:27:43,190
My bey, Selvi Hatun.

223
00:27:44,520 --> 00:27:46,500
She went to heaven.

224
00:27:55,270 --> 00:27:57,880
-My bey.
-Bala.

225
00:27:58,690 --> 00:28:00,620
Aygül.

226
00:28:02,470 --> 00:28:06,110
-Selvi?
-Selvi is a martyr, my bey.

227
00:28:09,080 --> 00:28:11,150
May Allah bless her.

228
00:28:11,530 --> 00:28:14,820
But there is something important
I need to tell you.

229
00:28:17,450 --> 00:28:19,200
Barkın Bey.

230
00:28:19,880 --> 00:28:21,610
Osman Bey.

231
00:28:29,960 --> 00:28:32,140
My condolences.

232
00:28:32,500 --> 00:28:34,410
Thank you, my bey.

233
00:28:35,900 --> 00:28:39,360
I heard that you brought the dog
who killed my wife.

234
00:28:40,420 --> 00:28:42,040
Is it true?

235
00:29:00,320 --> 00:29:03,050
My bey, did you find that dog?

236
00:29:03,050 --> 00:29:05,050
I have. I have.

237
00:29:07,860 --> 00:29:09,390
Osman Bey.

238
00:29:10,110 --> 00:29:14,650
You'll give me my Selvi's, revenge, right?

239
00:29:23,700 --> 00:29:28,510
When the time comes, his blood is yours.

240
00:29:29,610 --> 00:29:32,630
-Don't worry.
-Thank you.

241
00:29:34,700 --> 00:29:39,130
We have that weasel.
I'm relieved.

242
00:29:42,190 --> 00:29:45,130
You should too, Barkın Bey.

243
00:29:46,420 --> 00:29:49,230
My sister will be avenged.

244
00:29:55,910 --> 00:29:57,960
I know that you are in pain.

245
00:29:59,570 --> 00:30:02,180
But the beys will come
to the tent.

246
00:30:03,690 --> 00:30:05,810
You have to come as well.

247
00:30:06,030 --> 00:30:08,390
It is time for revenge, Osman Bey.

248
00:30:09,110 --> 00:30:10,640
I will come.

249
00:30:25,440 --> 00:30:28,390
Yeni Şehir

250
00:30:38,870 --> 00:30:40,580
Open the doors!

251
00:30:40,740 --> 00:30:42,610
Open the doors!

252
00:30:42,760 --> 00:30:45,310
Romanos and his army is coming!

253
00:30:56,030 --> 00:30:58,290
May God protect you, Romanos!

254
00:31:15,830 --> 00:31:21,450
-Welcome, Romanos!
-May God protect you, Romanos!

255
00:31:22,400 --> 00:31:29,190
-May God protect you, Romanos!
-Welcome, Romanos!

256
00:31:30,500 --> 00:31:33,290
The last unit has arrived.

257
00:31:35,600 --> 00:31:37,780
It seems so.

258
00:31:43,410 --> 00:31:46,450
We have to take care of this as soon as
possible.

259
00:32:21,870 --> 00:32:26,220
-Welcome!
-Welcome, Romanos!

260
00:32:45,880 --> 00:32:48,870
Brave soldiers of Rome!

261
00:32:49,900 --> 00:32:53,230
You have an important reason to be here
today!

262
00:32:54,720 --> 00:33:00,860
Arrogant Turks set their eyes on your
lands!

263
00:33:03,600 --> 00:33:06,500
So you survived, Romanos.

264
00:33:06,770 --> 00:33:12,150
So far, we have lost many lands because
of useless lords!

265
00:33:12,310 --> 00:33:18,510
Now, Osman's new goal is Bursa.

266
00:33:21,910 --> 00:33:24,880
And here is the gate to Bursa!

267
00:33:25,740 --> 00:33:27,380
Yeni Şehir!

268
00:33:27,940 --> 00:33:31,580
We must inform my Bey at once, Father.

269
00:33:31,580 --> 00:33:34,820
-But we...
-We must defeat this dog pack.

270
00:33:35,070 --> 00:33:37,680
...will protect Yeni Şehir!

271
00:33:37,930 --> 00:33:41,050
We won't let the Turks pass!

272
00:33:42,520 --> 00:33:47,040
Because, if we let the Turks pass
through here...

273
00:33:47,280 --> 00:33:49,850
...we will be betraying our history.

274
00:33:51,110 --> 00:33:53,520
Will the mighty soldier of Rome...

275
00:33:53,670 --> 00:33:55,720
...betray Rome?

276
00:33:55,950 --> 00:34:00,560
-He won't! He won't! He won't!
-He won't! He won't! He won't!

277
00:34:00,710 --> 00:34:03,260
Will the mighty soldier of Rome...

278
00:34:03,390 --> 00:34:05,189
...let the Turks pass?

279
00:34:05,350 --> 00:34:08,500
-He won't! He won't! He won't!
-He won't! He won't! He won't!

280
00:34:08,679 --> 00:34:12,929
May your sword be sharpened by your
hatred!

281
00:34:13,219 --> 00:34:15,989
We gift the every Turkish head we cut
off...

282
00:34:16,139 --> 00:34:18,438
...to Rome!

283
00:34:18,530 --> 00:34:34,389
-Long live Great Rome!
-Long live Great Rome!

284
00:34:34,520 --> 00:34:35,938
Beys.

285
00:34:36,460 --> 00:34:39,580
We gathered and discussed.

286
00:34:41,770 --> 00:34:45,159
We set the game and made a plan.

287
00:34:45,949 --> 00:34:48,510
From now on, there is no need for words.

288
00:34:49,620 --> 00:34:51,820
Tomorrow, we will set off and...

289
00:34:53,190 --> 00:34:56,179
...we will besiege Yeni Şehir.

290
00:34:59,830 --> 00:35:01,880
Can I come in, my Bey?

291
00:35:02,100 --> 00:35:04,530
Come in, Turahan.

292
00:35:09,250 --> 00:35:13,150
A messenger came from Çobanoğlu Ali Bey.

293
00:35:17,040 --> 00:35:18,510
Let him in.

294
00:35:29,850 --> 00:35:32,690
-May peace be upon you.
-May peace be upon you.

295
00:35:35,300 --> 00:35:36,840
Welcome.

296
00:35:38,460 --> 00:35:39,530
Tell me.

297
00:35:39,760 --> 00:35:41,090
I will.

298
00:35:41,800 --> 00:35:43,770
That's why I came, Osman Bey..

299
00:35:44,890 --> 00:35:47,530
Ali Bey sent me to remind you.

300
00:35:49,750 --> 00:35:57,280
My Bey wants his son Mustafa Bey and
Turgut Bey who is the killed of Atabey.

301
00:36:01,790 --> 00:36:06,470
If you don't give them, you will face
Ali Bey's wrath.

302
00:36:06,730 --> 00:36:07,990
Hey!

303
00:36:08,160 --> 00:36:09,600
Alps!

304
00:36:12,690 --> 00:36:14,150
Stop for a moment.

305
00:36:26,190 --> 00:36:28,590
Our cause is conquest.

306
00:36:30,790 --> 00:36:35,290
But you think about your personal agenda.

307
00:36:38,040 --> 00:36:39,310
So be it.

308
00:36:40,310 --> 00:36:45,020
Turgut Bey accepted giving his life for
this purpose.

309
00:36:46,280 --> 00:36:49,940
But he doesn't want anyone to prevent it.

310
00:36:52,440 --> 00:36:56,000
Thus, Tell Ali Bey that...

311
00:36:58,550 --> 00:37:03,420
...I will deliver Mustafa and Turgut Bey.

312
00:37:09,650 --> 00:37:11,710
How, my Bey?

313
00:37:11,730 --> 00:37:16,050
No. Stop.

314
00:37:19,470 --> 00:37:21,560
-Boran.
-Yes, my Bey.

315
00:37:22,710 --> 00:37:24,450
Accompany the messenger.

316
00:37:28,840 --> 00:37:30,350
As you order, my Bey.

317
00:37:31,510 --> 00:37:33,580
I will gladly forward this, Osman Bey.

318
00:37:39,220 --> 00:37:41,260
You made the right decision, Osman Bey.

319
00:37:41,720 --> 00:37:45,020
We must finalize these matters at once as
there is a conquest to make.

320
00:37:45,320 --> 00:37:46,950
This is what's right.

321
00:37:47,880 --> 00:37:50,600
We sacrificed Turgut Bey for the conquest.

322
00:37:52,080 --> 00:37:54,290
Even though I don't like it...

323
00:37:56,720 --> 00:37:58,380
...it will be.

324
00:38:01,690 --> 00:38:06,960
We will give Turgut Bey and take
Yeni Şehir.

325
00:38:11,360 --> 00:38:14,700
So, what is your move for Yeni Şehir,
my Bey?

326
00:38:19,410 --> 00:38:25,480
I will settle in the Akbıyık district near
Yeni Şehir with my alps.

327
00:38:26,620 --> 00:38:32,450
The others will take the valiants with
them and be with Konur.

328
00:38:33,640 --> 00:38:38,880
When we start the attack, you will come
right after us.

329
00:39:00,260 --> 00:39:02,040
Walk!

330
00:39:07,100 --> 00:39:08,760
Osman Bey!

331
00:39:10,640 --> 00:39:12,060
Walk!

332
00:39:18,600 --> 00:39:23,240
I was just coming to your tribe to convey
you the news from Ali Bey.

333
00:39:36,630 --> 00:39:44,130
Ali Bey wants his son Mustafa Bey and
Turgut Bey who is the killed of Atabey.

334
00:39:48,120 --> 00:39:52,400
Ali Bey will come with his army if you
don't agree.

335
00:39:55,110 --> 00:39:56,800
I couldn't hear you.

336
00:40:00,480 --> 00:40:04,130
Ali Bey will come with his army if you
don't agree.

337
00:40:06,000 --> 00:40:07,980
I couldn't hear you, messenger.

338
00:40:10,090 --> 00:40:13,230
I am just a messenger, Osman Bey.

339
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:21,880
Messenger, I will listen to you when you
come to my gathering.

340
00:40:22,790 --> 00:40:24,710
What do you mean, Osman Bey?

341
00:40:24,890 --> 00:40:29,230
Ali Bey doesn't see the truth. A game
is being played.

342
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:32,340
They are covering the truth.

343
00:40:33,640 --> 00:40:35,940
But I will uncover that truth.

344
00:40:37,630 --> 00:40:39,940
You will do as I say for this purpose.

345
00:40:40,350 --> 00:40:44,730
You will give your statement on front of
everyone as I say.

346
00:40:49,690 --> 00:40:53,490
Alps, take care of the messenger.

347
00:40:54,360 --> 00:40:56,210
No harm will come to him.

348
00:40:59,670 --> 00:41:00,880
Come on.

349
00:41:06,120 --> 00:41:09,640
How will Osman Bey manage this matter?

350
00:41:10,240 --> 00:41:12,960
You will know it when there is something
you need to know.

351
00:41:17,130 --> 00:41:18,900
You will be our guest for now.

352
00:41:36,170 --> 00:41:37,640
What does this mean?

353
00:41:38,100 --> 00:41:40,050
I did everything you told me to.

354
00:41:41,160 --> 00:41:42,980
It is Osman Bey's order.

355
00:41:43,770 --> 00:41:45,560
Earning his trust isn't easy

356
00:41:45,890 --> 00:41:50,840
You are already on bad terms with Ali Bey.
You are still trying him.

357
00:41:51,190 --> 00:41:53,210
This is disrespect!

358
00:41:54,030 --> 00:41:57,730
The real disrespect is to judge
without knowing the truth.

359
00:41:58,600 --> 00:42:04,890
Osman Bey doesn't trust Ali Bey, who is
infuriated and his messenger at all.

360
00:42:07,320 --> 00:42:11,570
Alps! Take our guests to the tent!

361
00:42:12,260 --> 00:42:14,430
Give them anything they need.

362
00:42:15,150 --> 00:42:16,920
The price for this will be heavy.

363
00:42:17,550 --> 00:42:20,320
The burden of the eye that does
not see the truth is heavy.

364
00:42:22,400 --> 00:42:25,070
Whoever is blind, let them pay for it,
messenger!

365
00:42:27,070 --> 00:42:28,390
Come on.

366
00:42:40,560 --> 00:42:42,340
So Barkın is a traitor?

367
00:42:42,910 --> 00:42:44,540
How, Bala?

368
00:42:46,040 --> 00:42:50,300
I know we aren't that close but we haven't
seen any evil from him all these years.

369
00:42:50,830 --> 00:42:55,600
If he was the enemy enough to betray us,
wouldn't we have seen it until today?

370
00:42:55,660 --> 00:43:00,720
You say so but Atabey Ahmet Bey was
Barkın's friend.

371
00:43:01,250 --> 00:43:03,170
He didn't say anything when they came.

372
00:43:03,170 --> 00:43:05,220
He didn't say anything when Atabey
died.

373
00:43:06,200 --> 00:43:08,150
Why did he keep silent all those times?

374
00:43:10,780 --> 00:43:12,270
What about Selvi?

375
00:43:14,250 --> 00:43:18,170
Selvi wouldn't do this to us even Barkın
had done, Bala.

376
00:43:18,280 --> 00:43:19,360
She wouldn't.

377
00:43:19,960 --> 00:43:21,520
She maybe didn't even know.

378
00:43:22,280 --> 00:43:26,910
But Osman was suspecting Atabey Ahmet.

379
00:43:27,330 --> 00:43:31,090
Also, you and me both know that Turgut
Bey wouldn't kill him.

380
00:43:31,620 --> 00:43:33,060
Right.

381
00:43:33,450 --> 00:43:37,070
But then who did? You said Barkın was
his friend.

382
00:43:40,550 --> 00:43:45,740
Selvi told Barkın that Turgut Bey
was going to İnegöl.

383
00:43:47,810 --> 00:43:49,120
Selvi did?

384
00:43:52,970 --> 00:43:55,230
So she was a spy?

385
00:43:58,830 --> 00:44:00,470
How could this have happened?

386
00:44:01,390 --> 00:44:03,130
She was my sister.

387
00:44:04,890 --> 00:44:07,140
She didn't do it on purpose, I suppose.

388
00:44:08,350 --> 00:44:10,150
She was very upset.

389
00:44:10,440 --> 00:44:13,020
Then, they learned the place of the ambush
from Barkın.

390
00:44:13,540 --> 00:44:17,160
Later, they killed Ahmet and blamed it on
Turgut Bey.

391
00:44:17,510 --> 00:44:21,750
Hence, Ali Bey, who was Osman Bey's
friend, became his enemy.

392
00:44:22,140 --> 00:44:24,390
They want to isolate us.

393
00:44:26,360 --> 00:44:29,420
For all these years we have fed enemies,
not friends.

394
00:44:29,830 --> 00:44:33,640
We've seen many traitors, Malhun. All of
them were unbelievable.

395
00:44:39,520 --> 00:44:43,520
What about Selvi? Did she know her husband
was a traitor?

396
00:44:44,150 --> 00:44:45,710
I don't think so.

397
00:44:47,120 --> 00:44:49,960
She wouldn't lie on her deathbed.

398
00:44:51,410 --> 00:44:54,160
She said what she had to and left.

399
00:44:54,850 --> 00:44:58,680
She thinks that her husband works for the
sake of the tribe.

400
00:44:58,880 --> 00:45:01,820
Oh, my beautiful sister!

401
00:45:02,010 --> 00:45:04,280
Who knows what he did behind us
all these years.

402
00:45:04,570 --> 00:45:06,720
Oh, my unfortunate sister!

403
00:45:09,180 --> 00:45:13,110
Let's go to Osman Bey at once. I couldn't
tell him yet.

404
00:45:14,940 --> 00:45:18,920
Let's go so that the traitor will be
punished as soon as possible.

405
00:45:19,620 --> 00:45:23,110
-Can I come in?
-Come in, my Bey!

406
00:45:33,230 --> 00:45:36,340
My Bey, we were coming to you.

407
00:45:36,890 --> 00:45:38,120
Tell me.

408
00:45:38,620 --> 00:45:42,080
My Bey, Selvi gave us crucial information.

409
00:45:56,800 --> 00:46:01,190
Don't worry, we won't stay here for long.

410
00:46:01,660 --> 00:46:05,470
You worked with Osman Bey while you could
just give Ali Bey's message.

411
00:46:09,030 --> 00:46:10,720
You know nothing!

412
00:46:11,710 --> 00:46:15,400
I had to. I didn't do it willingly.

413
00:46:16,950 --> 00:46:18,710
Know this!

414
00:46:30,270 --> 00:46:32,650
I shouldn't have trusted you, Osman Bey.

415
00:46:33,800 --> 00:46:35,330
I shouldn't have believed you.

416
00:46:38,890 --> 00:46:42,100
So you say Barkın is the traitor.

417
00:46:43,340 --> 00:46:45,430
Selvi confessed.

418
00:46:45,860 --> 00:46:49,500
She told Barkın that Turgut Bey
was leaving.

419
00:46:52,720 --> 00:46:57,580
Obviously, Barkın sent the news to his
close friend Ahmet Bey.

420
00:47:01,790 --> 00:47:03,000
So...

421
00:47:05,870 --> 00:47:07,820
...what else did Selvi Hatun say?

422
00:47:08,440 --> 00:47:10,840
She said that Barkın did all of this for
his tribe.

423
00:47:11,050 --> 00:47:12,680
And not to misunderstand him.

424
00:47:13,200 --> 00:47:14,680
But she was so uneasy.

425
00:47:15,020 --> 00:47:16,680
She kept asking for our blessings.

426
00:47:19,360 --> 00:47:21,610
Since she feels this guilty...

427
00:47:23,240 --> 00:47:24,600
...he's done huge mistakes.

428
00:47:28,620 --> 00:47:29,400
My Bey.

429
00:47:30,380 --> 00:47:33,870
Can Barkın be involved in the game set
against Turgut Bey.

430
00:47:35,930 --> 00:47:39,870
If he was, he must have hidden well.

431
00:47:41,180 --> 00:47:43,400
Selvi Hatun said he was friends with
Ahmet Bey.

432
00:47:45,120 --> 00:47:46,640
Did he kill his own friend?

433
00:47:47,500 --> 00:47:51,900
Is what Selvi Hatun said evidence of
Barkın Bey's treachery?

434
00:47:52,410 --> 00:47:54,070
He's been with us all these years.

435
00:47:54,070 --> 00:47:55,900
He didn't make a mistake as well.

436
00:47:56,280 --> 00:47:58,110
Why would he betray us now?

437
00:47:58,760 --> 00:48:01,920
Since he's done all these while looking
into our eyes...

438
00:48:06,090 --> 00:48:07,710
...he is capable of killing Ahmet.

439
00:48:09,370 --> 00:48:10,540
He is.

440
00:48:10,540 --> 00:48:12,200
A traitor doesn't need a reason.

441
00:48:13,260 --> 00:48:14,780
He must have a benefit.

442
00:48:17,400 --> 00:48:19,230
We will find all out.

443
00:48:20,700 --> 00:48:22,760
We will plan the game on Barkın.

444
00:48:25,240 --> 00:48:26,220
Aktemur.

445
00:48:26,960 --> 00:48:29,290
You will go to Ali Bey with Baysungur.

446
00:48:30,120 --> 00:48:31,290
Konur.

447
00:48:31,680 --> 00:48:34,000
You will take Mustafa and Turgut Bey.

448
00:48:36,170 --> 00:48:38,000
As for you, Cerkutay...

449
00:48:39,040 --> 00:48:41,110
...you will go after Hüsamettin and
Barkın.

450
00:48:41,360 --> 00:48:43,500
Keep your eyes on him.

451
00:48:44,250 --> 00:48:45,850
He will go to the funeral.

452
00:48:46,800 --> 00:48:48,600
If he is a traitor...

453
00:48:49,300 --> 00:48:51,080
...he will definitely send some news.

454
00:48:54,430 --> 00:48:55,900
As you order, my Bey.

455
00:49:00,670 --> 00:49:01,420
My Bey.

456
00:49:02,090 --> 00:49:04,300
The messenger is still captive.

457
00:49:04,520 --> 00:49:05,580
What about them?

458
00:49:07,870 --> 00:49:09,500
We will keep them.

459
00:49:10,160 --> 00:49:13,020
We will keep him until our plan works.

460
00:49:13,480 --> 00:49:14,480
As you order, my Bey.

461
00:49:15,230 --> 00:49:16,480
Here you go.

462
00:49:25,210 --> 00:49:26,570
Forgive me, my Bey.

463
00:49:27,840 --> 00:49:29,580
I got this traitor in the tribe.

464
00:49:29,930 --> 00:49:33,210
No, Malhun. You have no fault.

465
00:49:33,930 --> 00:49:35,210
They are hypocrites.

466
00:49:36,060 --> 00:49:37,590
They didn't deceive only you...

467
00:49:38,320 --> 00:49:39,970
...but all of us.

468
00:49:41,050 --> 00:49:42,300
Don't be hard on yourself.

469
00:49:46,910 --> 00:49:51,050
Now we are going to fulfill our last duty
to Selvi Hatun.

470
00:49:52,440 --> 00:49:53,360
Come on.

471
00:50:08,700 --> 00:50:11,530
The lord and Romanos are cautious.

472
00:50:12,700 --> 00:50:15,560
The number of soldiers increases
day by day.

473
00:50:18,200 --> 00:50:19,240
I found out today...

474
00:50:19,790 --> 00:50:23,400
...that healer women and nuns are
coming from İznik.

475
00:50:23,880 --> 00:50:25,880
They take precautions just in case.

476
00:50:28,360 --> 00:50:32,240
Healers and nuns...

477
00:50:37,760 --> 00:50:39,580
This is very important information.

478
00:50:41,280 --> 00:50:43,310
We will convey this to Osman Bey
at once.

479
00:50:43,760 --> 00:50:45,310
Immediately.

480
00:51:02,940 --> 00:51:05,640
-I am sorry for your loss, Barkın Bey.
-Thank you.

481
00:51:05,960 --> 00:51:08,430
-I am sorry for your loss, Barkın Bey.
-Thank you.

482
00:51:08,490 --> 00:51:10,170
-I am sorry for your loss.
-Thanks.

483
00:51:10,270 --> 00:51:15,100
-I am sorry for your loss, Barkın Bey.
-Thank you.

484
00:51:32,510 --> 00:51:33,720
Hüsamettin.

485
00:51:34,120 --> 00:51:34,970
Yes, my Bey?

486
00:51:35,310 --> 00:51:36,990
Go to Romanos.

487
00:51:39,280 --> 00:51:40,430
Tell him that...

488
00:51:41,710 --> 00:51:43,930
...Osman will attack Yeni Şehir.

489
00:51:45,070 --> 00:51:46,600
He will settle in Akbıyık...

490
00:51:47,660 --> 00:51:49,660
...with his closest alps.

491
00:51:51,310 --> 00:51:52,510
Tell him to...

492
00:51:53,290 --> 00:51:55,600
...kill Osman this time.

493
00:52:04,410 --> 00:52:05,530
Tell him that...

494
00:52:06,940 --> 00:52:09,790
...if he can't manage to kill Osman
again...

495
00:52:11,600 --> 00:52:15,920
...Barkın Bey won't leave him to Osman.

496
00:52:17,070 --> 00:52:18,700
He will kill you himself.

497
00:52:19,920 --> 00:52:20,940
As you order, my Bey.

498
00:52:24,680 --> 00:52:27,310
Let's see what you are up to.

499
00:52:28,060 --> 00:52:29,530
Barkın Bey and...

500
00:52:33,120 --> 00:52:34,040
...his dog.

501
00:52:44,000 --> 00:52:45,470
What took you from me...

502
00:52:46,840 --> 00:52:48,430
...wasn't the disease, my Selvi.

503
00:52:51,610 --> 00:52:54,220
It was the Kayı tribe.

504
00:52:57,450 --> 00:52:59,290
I will kill them all.

505
00:53:02,080 --> 00:53:03,310
Osman.

506
00:53:04,940 --> 00:53:06,400
Kayıs.

507
00:53:07,790 --> 00:53:11,470
And even that useless Romanos.

508
00:53:15,850 --> 00:53:18,220
I will take your revenge, my Selvi.

509
00:53:25,530 --> 00:53:27,180
I promise you.

510
00:53:30,440 --> 00:53:32,640
I promise you that...

511
00:53:34,640 --> 00:53:37,520
...I won't let any of them live.

512
00:53:40,410 --> 00:53:42,090
I will kill Osman.

513
00:53:44,560 --> 00:53:45,960
And his hatuns.

514
00:53:48,120 --> 00:53:49,600
And his children.

515
00:53:52,300 --> 00:53:54,190
I promise you, Selvi.

516
00:53:58,670 --> 00:54:00,510
I will kill them all.

517
00:54:20,090 --> 00:54:21,200
My baby.

518
00:54:22,780 --> 00:54:23,760
Mother.

519
00:54:25,180 --> 00:54:26,330
Father.

520
00:54:26,960 --> 00:54:29,580
My aunt Selvi won't return.

521
00:54:33,080 --> 00:54:34,890
Oh, my angel daughter.

522
00:54:43,130 --> 00:54:45,320
Make them forge my sword now, father.

523
00:54:45,580 --> 00:54:47,900
I will take my aunt Selvi's revenge!

524
00:54:51,880 --> 00:54:54,490
Come here. Come here.

525
00:54:55,210 --> 00:54:56,750
Come here.

526
00:55:03,580 --> 00:55:06,030
Son, bring it.

527
00:55:13,660 --> 00:55:15,000
My angel.

528
00:55:16,730 --> 00:55:17,920
My angel.

529
00:55:21,040 --> 00:55:22,320
Give it to me.

530
00:55:25,680 --> 00:55:27,070
Let me see it first.

531
00:56:18,240 --> 00:56:19,630
Good.

532
00:56:20,560 --> 00:56:21,630
Son.

533
00:56:26,560 --> 00:56:30,170
Praise be! It is exactly what I wanted.

534
00:56:37,280 --> 00:56:39,080
Since you forged it...

535
00:56:39,980 --> 00:56:41,550
...you will give it.

536
00:56:47,150 --> 00:56:50,520
We forged it together with your brother
Alaaddin, sister. It is yours.

537
00:56:52,110 --> 00:56:53,720
Thank you, brother.

538
00:57:33,720 --> 00:57:35,880
It suits you.

539
00:57:40,920 --> 00:57:41,880
Come on.

540
00:57:42,920 --> 00:57:44,480
Kiss your brother's hand.

541
00:57:59,370 --> 00:58:02,350
My beautiful girl. Be careful. All right?

542
00:58:02,880 --> 00:58:05,210
Draw your sword only at the enemy.

543
00:58:06,090 --> 00:58:10,010
Also, don't hold it and hurt yourself
before the training.

544
00:58:12,010 --> 00:58:13,950
You kept your promise, father.

545
00:58:15,260 --> 00:58:17,980
You must keep your promise as well,
my beautiful.

546
00:58:18,990 --> 00:58:20,800
Be a good sister to your brother.

547
00:58:21,520 --> 00:58:22,800
No jeaolusy.

548
00:58:25,000 --> 00:58:26,140
Come here.

549
00:58:26,360 --> 00:58:27,740
Come here, my Orhan.

550
00:58:28,190 --> 00:58:30,990
Come here, my Malhun.

551
00:58:57,370 --> 00:58:58,470
Osman Bey...

552
00:58:59,710 --> 00:59:04,030
...the soil on earth and the Great Tengri
in heaven are my witness that...

553
00:59:05,780 --> 00:59:09,080
...I am regretful.

554
00:59:11,970 --> 00:59:13,320
I only wanted gold.

555
00:59:21,760 --> 00:59:23,260
Don't you see my state?

556
00:59:24,600 --> 00:59:25,900
I am begging you!

557
00:59:28,020 --> 00:59:33,110
In the presence of Great Tengri, my wish
is that you forgive me, Osman Bey.

558
00:59:35,300 --> 00:59:37,520
A hungry man doesn't care who he works
for.

559
00:59:39,820 --> 00:59:41,990
You stay here still like a dog but...

560
00:59:42,760 --> 00:59:47,280
...whenever you open your mouth, dirt
comes out of your mouth.

561
00:59:49,540 --> 00:59:54,380
Dog barks louder when trapped.

562
00:59:56,100 --> 00:59:58,460
You are trapped as well.

563
01:00:00,320 --> 01:00:02,080
But let me tell you something.

564
01:00:05,140 --> 01:00:10,300
Your words mean nothing from now on.

565
01:00:12,360 --> 01:00:17,320
Back then, you added a Mongol
to your alps.

566
01:00:17,320 --> 01:00:20,800
I heard many times that
you fight as a Turk.

567
01:00:22,700 --> 01:00:27,220
As you trusted him.
As you took him.

568
01:00:27,970 --> 01:00:30,890
Spare me too, Osman Bey.

569
01:00:32,670 --> 01:00:34,590
You'll have another sword
serving you.

570
01:00:35,640 --> 01:00:37,050
Do you know the pharoah?

571
01:00:39,410 --> 01:00:41,650
When he denied Hz. Moses...

572
01:00:43,300 --> 01:00:47,500
when he realised that he'll get drowned,
he said that he believed.

573
01:00:50,250 --> 01:00:52,890
But his faith wasn't real.

574
01:00:53,800 --> 01:00:59,160
Yours is just like the pharoah.

575
01:01:01,890 --> 01:01:06,160
So, don't expect any mercy
from me.

576
01:01:07,060 --> 01:01:09,860
You surrounded when you had
nowhere to run.

577
01:01:11,350 --> 01:01:16,540
Our followers' swords should
shine with light of faith.

578
01:01:19,140 --> 01:01:22,580
May I enter, my bey?
Barkın Bey is here.

579
01:01:23,660 --> 01:01:24,580
Come.

580
01:01:49,310 --> 01:01:51,950
My bey, Osman Bey's nephew Aktemur
is here.

581
01:01:51,950 --> 01:01:52,980
He has news.

582
01:01:55,820 --> 01:01:59,330
Aktemur! Murderer of my son!

583
01:02:09,500 --> 01:02:12,950
You! You killed me son!

584
01:02:12,950 --> 01:02:14,070
Kill him!

585
01:02:48,480 --> 01:02:50,310
I didn't kill your son!

586
01:02:51,860 --> 01:02:53,190
Your son is alive!

587
01:02:55,950 --> 01:02:58,170
I brought you news from Osman Bey.

588
01:03:16,510 --> 01:03:19,350
I came here as an envoy.

589
01:03:20,960 --> 01:03:22,980
My life is under your protection.

590
01:03:25,500 --> 01:03:27,230
Where is my envoy, Aktemur?

591
01:03:28,620 --> 01:03:31,260
If he is alive, where is my son?

592
01:03:32,990 --> 01:03:35,750
Osman Bey is hosting him because
he is tired.

593
01:03:36,350 --> 01:03:38,110
They'll come with my bey.

594
01:03:39,910 --> 01:03:44,260
If Osman makes another mistake...

595
01:03:46,080 --> 01:03:48,060
if he hurts my envoy...

596
01:03:48,060 --> 01:03:50,060
We said that your envoy is
our guest.

597
01:03:50,290 --> 01:03:52,060
They are treating him the best way.

598
01:03:55,530 --> 01:03:58,520
And we are hoping that you'll
do the same.

599
01:04:00,720 --> 01:04:04,840
Ali Bey, your son was impudent again.

600
01:04:06,280 --> 01:04:08,440
And Aktemur Bey gave him a lesson.

601
01:04:10,180 --> 01:04:15,470
But don't worry. He is alive.

602
01:04:15,900 --> 01:04:21,590
I didn't give you a lesson when you
were impudent.

603
01:04:22,830 --> 01:04:24,370
Now be silent!

604
01:04:26,270 --> 01:04:27,460
Let the envoy speak.

605
01:04:30,320 --> 01:04:31,970
What does Osman Bey say?

606
01:04:32,980 --> 01:04:36,380
He wanted you to know that he'll
bring Turgut Bey personally tomorrow.

607
01:04:36,810 --> 01:04:39,360
Your son will be there too,
safe and sound.

608
01:04:40,040 --> 01:04:44,060
Osman Bey will serve justice.

609
01:04:47,540 --> 01:04:53,900
I was thinking that the Kayı learned
nothing from their ancestors.

610
01:04:54,960 --> 01:04:59,520
But Osman is coming round.

611
01:05:01,060 --> 01:05:05,050
The Kayı stood with justice yesterday
as they'll tomorrow.

612
01:05:05,830 --> 01:05:07,820
The Kayı never changed, Ali Bey.

613
01:05:08,750 --> 01:05:13,720
But you are blinded to the truth when it
doesn't match with your profits.

614
01:05:15,140 --> 01:05:19,870
But don't worry. Justice of the Kayı
will open all the blind eyes.

615
01:05:26,620 --> 01:05:29,510
Take our guest to his room.

616
01:05:51,680 --> 01:05:53,870
Did this man kill my Selvi?

617
01:05:59,810 --> 01:06:00,680
He did.

618
01:06:04,410 --> 01:06:10,480
Washing this dog in blood is
your right.

619
01:06:27,650 --> 01:06:29,640
You took Selvi from me.

620
01:06:29,640 --> 01:06:30,670
Forgive me.

621
01:06:33,060 --> 01:06:34,380
Show mercy!

622
01:06:41,150 --> 01:06:42,690
No mercy.

623
01:06:47,520 --> 01:06:49,740
You took Selvi from me...

624
01:07:02,170 --> 01:07:04,090
and I took your life.

625
01:07:28,210 --> 01:07:30,850
İnegöl Castle

626
01:07:31,270 --> 01:07:33,030
I came to take Mustafa.

627
01:07:33,790 --> 01:07:35,970
It's the end of your visit, shehzad.

628
01:07:51,890 --> 01:07:53,300
Turgut!

629
01:08:00,830 --> 01:08:04,580
If you be impudent,
I'll take your life!

630
01:08:07,370 --> 01:08:11,070
Turgut Bey, you need to come
with us too.

631
01:08:12,370 --> 01:08:14,179
We'll give you to Ali Bey.

632
01:08:18,710 --> 01:08:20,439
It's Osman Bey's order.

633
01:08:29,599 --> 01:08:32,929
What happened, Turgut Bey?

634
01:08:32,929 --> 01:08:36,929
You were speaking highly.
Now you got what you deserve.

635
01:08:37,830 --> 01:08:40,279
But your bey understood
what you are made of.

636
01:08:40,920 --> 01:08:42,649
He understood and sold you.

637
01:08:43,460 --> 01:08:48,479
I wish you knew what I'll do to
you.

638
01:08:53,099 --> 01:08:55,269
I know myself, Konur.

639
01:08:55,269 --> 01:08:57,538
I won't surrender for something
I didn't do!

640
01:08:57,538 --> 01:08:59,580
And not because of this boy's
slander.

641
01:09:07,240 --> 01:09:11,309
But my Osman brother's order
will be followed.

642
01:09:14,149 --> 01:09:17,059
Who are you to get listened, Turgut?

643
01:09:17,109 --> 01:09:22,059
Osman Bey tells you to come and you come.
He tells you to go and you go.

644
01:09:24,510 --> 01:09:26,410
When the truth gets revealed...

645
01:09:27,450 --> 01:09:30,300
we'll see what water can
wash your dirt.

646
01:09:31,290 --> 01:09:35,889
Don't give me advice, Turgut.
What do you know?

647
01:09:38,279 --> 01:09:40,540
You killed an innocent!

648
01:09:40,540 --> 01:09:43,800
Traitor! Murderer!

649
01:09:48,870 --> 01:09:50,120
Turgut Bey.

650
01:09:51,649 --> 01:09:54,060
Osman Bey expects you both
safe and sound.

651
01:10:02,370 --> 01:10:05,180
Both Gündoğan and I will come, Konur.

652
01:10:07,980 --> 01:10:09,240
Both of us.

653
01:10:14,940 --> 01:10:17,960
YENİ ŞEHİR

654
01:10:27,940 --> 01:10:29,540
So, tell me.

655
01:10:30,650 --> 01:10:32,810
What news have you
brought from Barkın Bey?

656
01:10:33,350 --> 01:10:35,430
He is going to deliver Osman Turgut.

657
01:10:43,100 --> 01:10:46,650
Because of Turgut, Kayıs and
Chobanids almost got into a fight.

658
01:10:48,970 --> 01:10:51,180
Osman took that opportunity
away from us.

659
01:10:51,740 --> 01:10:54,650
He is going to destroy our entire plan...

660
01:10:55,440 --> 01:10:57,540
...by giving away his most trusted man...

661
01:10:57,540 --> 01:10:59,840
...at the expense of destroying
our reputation.

662
01:10:59,840 --> 01:11:01,510
After delivering Turgut...

663
01:11:01,860 --> 01:11:03,640
...he'll attack Yeni Şehir.

664
01:11:06,220 --> 01:11:07,220
Osman.

665
01:11:08,260 --> 01:11:10,230
Osman. Osman.

666
01:11:15,430 --> 01:11:18,920
If Osman delivers Turgut...

667
01:11:20,360 --> 01:11:22,710
...Beys won't have any
trust for him no more.

668
01:11:24,040 --> 01:11:27,430
They'll think they'll be let
down at the first opportunity.

669
01:11:30,220 --> 01:11:33,110
Does he still want to
fight on these terms?

670
01:11:35,110 --> 01:11:36,300
Let him come.

671
01:11:47,800 --> 01:11:51,060
What are the battle plans?
The condition of the soldiers?

672
01:11:51,900 --> 01:11:54,950
Osman will arrive at
Akbih spot with his alps.

673
01:11:56,180 --> 01:11:58,720
Barıkın Bey says it's a proper
location for an ambush.

674
01:11:58,720 --> 01:12:01,360
He says they should strike
before they settle in well.

675
01:12:01,360 --> 01:12:02,940
Beys will come from behind.

676
01:12:03,220 --> 01:12:05,180
When Osman dies they won't matter.

677
01:12:05,910 --> 01:12:07,180
Good.

678
01:12:08,330 --> 01:12:09,690
Then, be ready.

679
01:12:11,180 --> 01:12:13,620
I'm going to set the
cruelest trap for him.

680
01:12:14,620 --> 01:12:17,400
Osman thinks he's coming
to expand his lands.

681
01:12:18,700 --> 01:12:20,570
But I'll burn him...

682
01:12:21,080 --> 01:12:24,980
...and mix his ashes with
the lands he's trying to take.

683
01:12:25,450 --> 01:12:29,000
Barkın Bey also says...

684
01:12:30,150 --> 01:12:32,060
...this is the last chance for Romanos.

685
01:12:33,500 --> 01:12:35,780
If he can't manage to
kill Osman once again...

686
01:12:37,020 --> 01:12:38,710
...I'll kill Romanos myself.

687
01:12:42,860 --> 01:12:45,220
Then, you tell your Bey...

688
01:12:47,800 --> 01:12:52,680
...that Akbıyık will become Osman's grave.

689
01:13:13,050 --> 01:13:15,030
Enjoy it, my valiant.

690
01:13:15,260 --> 01:13:17,110
May Allah bless you!

691
01:13:17,540 --> 01:13:19,430
I followed Barkın's man.

692
01:13:19,430 --> 01:13:21,430
He brought me all the way here.

693
01:13:22,520 --> 01:13:24,790
That reprobate.

694
01:13:27,320 --> 01:13:28,580
It seems...

695
01:13:29,260 --> 01:13:32,650
...that he'll send word to that
Romanos scoundrel, Hüsamettin.

696
01:13:34,970 --> 01:13:36,660
What are you saying, Davut Usta?

697
01:13:37,850 --> 01:13:39,660
Romanos was here.

698
01:13:40,090 --> 01:13:42,230
He'll be the commander
in chief of the army.

699
01:13:42,780 --> 01:13:44,540
Damn dogs!

700
01:13:44,540 --> 01:13:46,540
They're getting prepared.

701
01:13:46,760 --> 01:13:49,620
They also brought herbalists
and nuns from İznik.

702
01:13:57,130 --> 01:14:00,760
I should go and inform
my Bey about all of this.

703
01:14:01,960 --> 01:14:03,240
Thank you both!

704
01:14:03,690 --> 01:14:08,070
But, I won't leave that
Hüsamettin dog alone.

705
01:14:08,950 --> 01:14:10,280
Thank you!

706
01:14:10,780 --> 01:14:13,660
Cerkutay, may Allah help you!

707
01:14:13,830 --> 01:14:15,660
May he protect you!

708
01:14:15,860 --> 01:14:17,660
Thank you!

709
01:14:18,460 --> 01:14:22,460
You put your lives in danger
on enemy soil for war.

710
01:14:22,890 --> 01:14:24,730
May Allah bless you!

711
01:14:31,610 --> 01:14:32,630
May...

712
01:14:33,590 --> 01:14:35,340
May Allah help us!

713
01:14:37,450 --> 01:14:38,600
I should go.

714
01:14:39,860 --> 01:14:42,300
Let's go. Let's go.

715
01:14:52,040 --> 01:14:54,210
Are you better now, even just a bit?

716
01:14:55,610 --> 01:14:57,050
The death of Selvi...

717
01:14:58,170 --> 01:15:00,660
...will keep hurting me
for the rest of my life.

718
01:15:01,980 --> 01:15:02,860
But...

719
01:15:04,410 --> 01:15:06,780
...knowing that...

720
01:15:07,610 --> 01:15:10,140
...that dog is dead...

721
01:15:14,600 --> 01:15:15,960
...comforts me, Osman Bey.

722
01:15:18,580 --> 01:15:21,540
But, I haven't gotten what I wanted.

723
01:15:23,740 --> 01:15:27,240
There is a traitor amongst the
beys that are in my command.

724
01:15:31,100 --> 01:15:32,740
And collaborates with Cebe.

725
01:15:34,540 --> 01:15:35,660
If so...

726
01:15:36,600 --> 01:15:38,680
...why did you make me kill that dog?

727
01:15:39,500 --> 01:15:42,550
We could have made him speak, my Bey.

728
01:15:43,500 --> 01:15:47,020
Do you put your tribe in
danger to comfort me?

729
01:15:49,020 --> 01:15:49,960
Maybe,...

730
01:15:52,520 --> 01:15:53,900
...I didn't feel the need to.

731
01:15:56,820 --> 01:15:57,720
Or,...

732
01:15:59,720 --> 01:16:02,790
...the death of that dog gave me
more than enough information.

733
01:16:03,620 --> 01:16:04,790
Good then.

734
01:16:05,750 --> 01:16:09,930
If you know who he is, you can punish him.

735
01:16:10,650 --> 01:16:16,060
Neither Kayı nor Kızılbey Oğulları
will suffer this kind of pain again.

736
01:16:16,540 --> 01:16:19,700
But, tell me Osman Bey...

737
01:16:20,660 --> 01:16:25,020
...does that dog have anything
to do with the death of Selvi?

738
01:16:26,140 --> 01:16:27,270
Is he the only one?

739
01:16:29,500 --> 01:16:30,650
I'll ask.

740
01:16:31,400 --> 01:16:32,650
I'll ask all of it.

741
01:16:33,560 --> 01:16:35,180
Don't worry at all.

742
01:16:37,060 --> 01:16:38,740
Now that Cebe is dead...

743
01:16:40,740 --> 01:16:42,420
...someone else will talk.

744
01:16:44,180 --> 01:16:46,120
Who is that traitor?

745
01:16:47,110 --> 01:16:48,650
Romanos and Cebe.

746
01:16:52,090 --> 01:16:53,850
They all work for the same person.

747
01:16:56,570 --> 01:16:58,060
Now that Cebe is dead...

748
01:16:59,910 --> 01:17:01,540
...Romanos will speak.

749
01:17:06,760 --> 01:17:07,750
By the way...

750
01:17:09,580 --> 01:17:11,190
...the enemies outside...

751
01:17:12,730 --> 01:17:14,460
...and the traitor inside...

752
01:17:17,900 --> 01:17:20,730
...will not be able to prevent
the conquests, Barkın Bey.

753
01:17:22,700 --> 01:17:25,180
We're going to take Yeni Şehir.

754
01:17:51,240 --> 01:17:54,390
Mother, when is he going to kick?

755
01:17:55,670 --> 01:17:57,400
There is more time for that, son.

756
01:17:57,750 --> 01:17:58,790
He's too little.

757
01:17:59,240 --> 01:18:00,950
You ask like you don't know.

758
01:18:01,460 --> 01:18:03,740
What? You seem excited.

759
01:18:04,070 --> 01:18:05,740
I know but I can't wait, mother.

760
01:18:06,180 --> 01:18:09,150
I want him to come out and
grow up quickly if Allah permits.

761
01:18:09,190 --> 01:18:10,920
If Allah permits, Alaaddin.

762
01:18:13,130 --> 01:18:14,420
If Allah permits.

763
01:18:16,630 --> 01:18:18,860
Uncle Gündüz will also have a baby...

764
01:18:19,480 --> 01:18:20,540
...I get upset.

765
01:18:21,420 --> 01:18:23,580
But he'll be our brother as well.

766
01:18:24,330 --> 01:18:26,660
I'll tell him the heroic
deeds of my uncle.

767
01:18:27,050 --> 01:18:28,170
That's right.

768
01:18:29,380 --> 01:18:31,110
It is a test, Alaaddin.

769
01:18:31,700 --> 01:18:33,970
Your sheik grandfather
probably has told you.

770
01:18:33,990 --> 01:18:36,230
Everybody has a different test.

771
01:18:39,100 --> 01:18:42,300
My good-hearted brave son.

772
01:18:44,500 --> 01:18:46,420
So, tell me...

773
01:18:46,740 --> 01:18:48,300
...how is the training going?

774
01:18:48,650 --> 01:18:51,430
Do you want to have weapons
training with your mother?

775
01:18:51,740 --> 01:18:55,860
I don't have the ability yet to
draw on Bala Hatun, mother.

776
01:18:56,070 --> 01:18:57,320
I know my place.

777
01:19:13,100 --> 01:19:15,300
- My Osman.
- Alaaddin.

778
01:19:17,380 --> 01:19:19,020
Alaaddin.

779
01:19:24,470 --> 01:19:25,900
Come.

780
01:19:27,670 --> 01:19:29,020
Come.

781
01:19:29,930 --> 01:19:31,690
My smart boy.

782
01:19:32,180 --> 01:19:37,110
He knows very well that drawing
on Bala Hatun is not that easy.

783
01:19:39,500 --> 01:19:40,630
But,...

784
01:19:41,110 --> 01:19:44,170
...her eyes are sharper
than any weapon, son.

785
01:19:51,660 --> 01:19:53,110
You look tired, my Bey.

786
01:19:53,110 --> 01:19:54,390
No.

787
01:19:54,710 --> 01:19:58,740
Whenever I stroke the hair of my
kids and look into their eyes...

788
01:19:59,450 --> 01:20:01,510
...tiredness goes away.

789
01:20:02,790 --> 01:20:03,660
Alaaddin,...

790
01:20:04,650 --> 01:20:07,770
...- you'll have another brother, son.
- That's right, father.

791
01:20:08,660 --> 01:20:09,770
I can't wait.

792
01:20:10,120 --> 01:20:12,090
The time isn't passing for me.

793
01:20:12,220 --> 01:20:14,090
Same with me.

794
01:20:15,160 --> 01:20:16,820
It's not passing.

795
01:20:18,870 --> 01:20:22,680
All of my children give me
a different excitement.

796
01:20:23,940 --> 01:20:24,970
But, I...

797
01:20:26,100 --> 01:20:27,510
...love all of you.

798
01:20:29,020 --> 01:20:32,020
Make sure you also love and
protect each other as well.

799
01:20:32,170 --> 01:20:36,570
My brothers are in my hands, father.

800
01:20:36,890 --> 01:20:38,570
Praise be!

801
01:20:40,900 --> 01:20:42,580
Come.

802
01:20:43,820 --> 01:20:45,380
You come too.

803
01:20:47,060 --> 01:20:48,470
You come too.

804
01:20:58,250 --> 01:20:59,030
Mother.

805
01:20:59,640 --> 01:21:00,420
Aunt Ayşe.

806
01:21:00,900 --> 01:21:02,420
Aren't you pregnant?

807
01:21:02,780 --> 01:21:04,550
What are you doing in battle?

808
01:21:06,740 --> 01:21:10,040
Don't be afraid, son. We
have a different task.

809
01:21:11,510 --> 01:21:12,340
Alaaddin,...

810
01:21:13,300 --> 01:21:17,350
...do you know how many times your mother
fought when she had you in her belly?

811
01:21:18,740 --> 01:21:20,980
That's where your skills come from.

812
01:21:21,500 --> 01:21:24,230
You started learning
in your mother's belly.

813
01:21:26,060 --> 01:21:29,540
It's not that big of a
battle, don't worry.

814
01:21:29,830 --> 01:21:32,680
I'll go with Bacıyans and
protect your mother.

815
01:21:33,430 --> 01:21:35,590
She'll come back safe if Allah permits.

816
01:21:38,580 --> 01:21:39,500
If Allah permits.

817
01:21:42,120 --> 01:21:43,510
Praise be, hatuns!

818
01:21:44,170 --> 01:21:46,100
You're already prepared.

819
01:21:47,270 --> 01:21:51,720
Bala, Ayşe, it would be
beneficial to be careful.

820
01:21:53,510 --> 01:21:56,360
You say that to them but
your arm is wounded, mother.

821
01:21:59,600 --> 01:22:01,160
Don't you worry.

822
01:22:01,160 --> 01:22:04,570
Boys, you may be baffled and think...

823
01:22:04,910 --> 01:22:07,660
...why are they going
to battle in this state?

824
01:22:08,840 --> 01:22:10,210
Mothers get tired.

825
01:22:11,220 --> 01:22:14,500
They get hurt, but they don't give up.

826
01:22:16,010 --> 01:22:16,760
For what?

827
01:22:18,340 --> 01:22:20,980
So that you could wake
up to a better morning.

828
01:22:23,420 --> 01:22:27,100
Now, your job is to stay
here and pray for us.

829
01:22:27,100 --> 01:22:28,190
Isn't that right?

830
01:22:29,230 --> 01:22:31,570
That's right. Pray.

831
01:22:31,570 --> 01:22:33,990
Pray so that we could come back safely.

832
01:22:39,400 --> 01:22:41,430
Come on, I'm ready!

833
01:22:43,430 --> 01:22:44,660
What are we waiting for?

834
01:22:44,660 --> 01:22:47,560
It's the order of Osman Bey.
Let's not wait.

835
01:22:50,430 --> 01:22:54,060
My beautiful daughter,
didn't we talk about this?

836
01:22:55,420 --> 01:22:56,730
You're too litte.

837
01:22:57,470 --> 01:23:01,260
When it's time, aunt Bala
will have you join Bacıyans.

838
01:23:01,330 --> 01:23:03,410
But not now.

839
01:23:03,930 --> 01:23:04,810
Then, I'll go.

840
01:23:27,030 --> 01:23:29,550
You go, we'll pray for you.

841
01:23:31,070 --> 01:23:31,980
Right, sister?

842
01:23:35,660 --> 01:23:40,170
Before a battle, the kids should
pray for their mothers and fathers.

843
01:23:42,840 --> 01:23:44,560
You are right my big brothers.

844
01:23:47,020 --> 01:23:49,550
Let's pray so that they
can come back safely.

845
01:24:05,650 --> 01:24:08,140
He met with Romanos in Yeni Şehir.

846
01:24:09,080 --> 01:24:11,950
You said whoever works
with him is the traitor.

847
01:24:12,380 --> 01:24:15,950
- We'll find him if Allah permits, my bey.
- If Allah permits.

848
01:24:22,140 --> 01:24:25,280
He may be up to something
behind Barkın's back, my bey.

849
01:24:25,280 --> 01:24:27,280
We should be sure.

850
01:24:28,130 --> 01:24:32,180
We'll learn. We'll learn, Cerkutay.

851
01:24:32,180 --> 01:24:34,180
You go to Bala, now.

852
01:24:55,650 --> 01:24:58,180
The Osman who doesn't
know his place is here.

853
01:25:09,860 --> 01:25:14,130
My father will cut your head
off after Turgut, as well.

854
01:25:14,890 --> 01:25:16,960
You went too far.

855
01:25:28,520 --> 01:25:31,150
Why did you rush?

856
01:25:31,940 --> 01:25:35,920
You don't have to hit me for
me to cut your head off, Konur.

857
01:25:36,780 --> 01:25:40,010
You wait for your turn.

858
01:25:42,830 --> 01:25:44,840
We say we want to go forward...

859
01:25:46,840 --> 01:25:49,010
...your ancestor comes
and stands behind us.

860
01:25:50,510 --> 01:25:53,470
That dog Ata Bey with you...

861
01:25:54,570 --> 01:25:56,510
...collaborates with the enemy.

862
01:25:58,080 --> 01:26:00,650
Just so Ali Bey doesn't stand behind us.

863
01:26:03,870 --> 01:26:07,810
Of course, he will. He
is the enemy after all.

864
01:26:08,700 --> 01:26:10,270
That's his nature.

865
01:26:12,920 --> 01:26:15,490
But you know what's bad?

866
01:26:17,060 --> 01:26:19,230
Adding fuel to the flame.

867
01:26:20,830 --> 01:26:26,260
Forgetting your cause for
your own self-interest.

868
01:26:28,770 --> 01:26:35,110
You work with the devil without knowing
what you're doing and aiding the enemy.

869
01:26:41,570 --> 01:26:44,290
It's good that there aren't
many of you among Turkmen.

870
01:26:45,460 --> 01:26:47,700
Turkmens always side with us.

871
01:26:48,080 --> 01:26:51,980
They get heartened by our victory
and be proud of our conquest.

872
01:26:54,030 --> 01:26:59,650
But, thank goodness that
Ali Bey thinks that way as well.

873
01:27:02,430 --> 01:27:04,220
He's just being played.

874
01:27:10,640 --> 01:27:14,070
Alps, on your horses.

875
01:27:43,960 --> 01:27:45,050
Aktemur.

876
01:27:46,520 --> 01:27:50,050
I like and respect your
ancestor and your uncle.

877
01:27:51,690 --> 01:27:56,990
But if they try to play me...

878
01:27:57,530 --> 01:28:01,960
...the first head to be cut
off is yours, know that.

879
01:28:12,680 --> 01:28:14,230
My Bey, they're coming!

880
01:28:49,040 --> 01:28:50,180
Ali Bey.

881
01:28:56,010 --> 01:28:57,370
Osman Bey.

882
01:28:58,870 --> 01:29:07,610
Come on, deliver my son and Turgut Bey.

883
01:29:11,600 --> 01:29:13,120
Be patient.

884
01:29:14,670 --> 01:29:16,150
Be patient.

885
01:29:21,370 --> 01:29:23,260
YENİ ŞEHİR

886
01:29:23,920 --> 01:29:26,200
The army is ready, let's get on the road.

887
01:29:33,000 --> 01:29:37,010
Commander Romanos is
waiting, be quick, blacksmith.

888
01:29:42,530 --> 01:29:43,630
Blacksmith.

889
01:29:45,530 --> 01:29:48,580
I'll nail those horseshoes
on your skull! Be quick!

890
01:29:54,600 --> 01:29:56,650
Will this army be able to stop the Tuks?

891
01:29:57,790 --> 01:29:59,560
Yeni Şehir doesn't even have walls.

892
01:30:00,480 --> 01:30:02,470
Yeni Şehir may not have walls.

893
01:30:02,870 --> 01:30:06,850
But with the trap, I'll set up for them,
Osman won't even be able to come close...

894
01:30:06,850 --> 01:30:07,850
...to the city.

895
01:30:42,670 --> 01:30:43,710
Ali Bey.

896
01:30:44,620 --> 01:30:47,210
I told you there was something
going on with this job.

897
01:30:48,020 --> 01:30:50,290
I told you not to lose
control of your anger.

898
01:30:52,010 --> 01:30:54,800
I told you to wake up from
the sleep of heedlessness.

899
01:30:56,700 --> 01:31:01,410
But, I will awake you from
the sleep of heedlessness.

900
01:31:03,350 --> 01:31:08,620
The Ata Bey Ahmet who
disguised as one of my alps.

901
01:31:10,140 --> 01:31:11,870
He collaborated with the Mongols.

902
01:31:15,160 --> 01:31:22,030
That's why he was the one who
attacked Mustafa with Turgut Bey.

903
01:31:26,170 --> 01:31:27,730
But there are two more people.

904
01:31:29,240 --> 01:31:31,920
One of them is Romanos, the other is Cebe.

905
01:31:35,280 --> 01:31:39,180
Cebe is on the ground right now.
Romanos doesn't have much time either.

906
01:31:41,050 --> 01:31:42,900
Let's get to the main point.

907
01:31:43,500 --> 01:31:47,410
Ata Bey Ahmet was also
in collaboration with them.

908
01:31:50,910 --> 01:31:55,170
But, what they were
doing caused his demise.

909
01:31:57,350 --> 01:32:00,210
What are you talking about, Osman Bey?

910
01:32:00,210 --> 01:32:05,230
Ali Bey, they're doing all of this
just so you don't side with us.

911
01:32:06,200 --> 01:32:08,140
They wish to prevent the conquests.

912
01:32:08,480 --> 01:32:10,650
They wish to weaken Kayı.

913
01:32:12,670 --> 01:32:13,880
That's why...

914
01:32:17,100 --> 01:32:18,810
...they set up Turgut Bey.

915
01:32:22,590 --> 01:32:25,630
But there is one other person
who's also involved in this.

916
01:32:31,230 --> 01:32:32,670
About him...

917
01:32:37,630 --> 01:32:39,090
...he...

918
01:32:43,510 --> 01:32:45,880
...he is Barkın.

919
01:32:49,760 --> 01:32:54,170
Come here, come here, you
black sheep of Turkmen!

920
01:32:58,270 --> 01:32:59,470
What is wrong, Osman?

921
01:33:01,000 --> 01:33:04,210
Are you going to slander me to
get yourself out of this situation?

922
01:33:04,640 --> 01:33:07,010
Are you going to burn me
in order to save Turgut?

923
01:33:07,010 --> 01:33:08,010
Shut up!

924
01:33:09,760 --> 01:33:12,080
You won't speak unless I tell you to!

925
01:33:18,510 --> 01:33:19,760
Ali Bey,...

926
01:33:24,420 --> 01:33:26,200
...you're going to tell everything.

927
01:33:29,150 --> 01:33:30,380
Start talking.

928
01:33:39,620 --> 01:33:41,760
- Boran!
- I'm on it, my Bey.

929
01:34:22,250 --> 01:34:23,360
Hüsamettin!

930
01:34:25,520 --> 01:34:29,220
Where are wandering off to like a
cowardly dog trying to escape his fate?

931
01:34:35,760 --> 01:34:37,500
Run, Hüsamettin, run.

932
01:34:38,870 --> 01:34:41,040
It's been a while since
I hunted a traitor.

933
01:34:41,520 --> 01:34:43,130
There you go.

934
01:34:51,250 --> 01:34:52,610
Run, traitor.

935
01:34:55,490 --> 01:34:56,510
Run.

936
01:34:57,890 --> 01:34:59,190
- Baysungur.
- My bey?

937
01:34:59,820 --> 01:35:00,890
Bring him.

938
01:35:05,450 --> 01:35:06,480
This Barkın...

939
01:35:08,020 --> 01:35:11,380
...didn't even shy away from
sacrificing his partner Ahmet....

940
01:35:11,380 --> 01:35:13,240
...for his moves.

941
01:35:14,690 --> 01:35:18,650
And from making his
wife Selvi a spy against us.

942
01:35:20,570 --> 01:35:21,790
Mustafa,...

943
01:35:23,590 --> 01:35:24,700
...tell me...

944
01:35:25,290 --> 01:35:27,590
...who told you the
location of Turgut Bey?

945
01:35:34,080 --> 01:35:35,100
Mustafa!

946
01:35:37,250 --> 01:35:38,340
Tell us!

947
01:35:40,090 --> 01:35:41,230
Barkın Bey did.

948
01:35:50,980 --> 01:35:53,140
Barkın's friendship
with Ahmet is apparent.

949
01:35:53,760 --> 01:35:56,380
And it's obvious that he
is a part of this scheme.

950
01:35:57,020 --> 01:35:58,590
Now admit it yourself.

951
01:35:59,490 --> 01:36:01,970
Admit what, Osman? What?

952
01:36:04,200 --> 01:36:06,790
I've never been part of
a treacherous act, but...

953
01:36:08,280 --> 01:36:10,120
...I'll make you pay for this.

954
01:36:13,790 --> 01:36:15,780
I am not a traitor!

955
01:36:15,940 --> 01:36:16,970
Shut up!

956
01:36:19,880 --> 01:36:21,230
You're not a traitor?

957
01:36:22,820 --> 01:36:24,130
You're not a traitor?

958
01:37:10,220 --> 01:37:11,410
Hüsamettin.

959
01:37:19,930 --> 01:37:20,960
Boran.

960
01:37:21,760 --> 01:37:23,920
Boran, you will die!

961
01:37:36,230 --> 01:37:38,690
Attacks helplessly when
backed into a corner.

962
01:37:39,630 --> 01:37:40,720
Come here.

963
01:37:46,780 --> 01:37:48,420
You don't have the heart, Boran.

964
01:37:49,630 --> 01:37:52,530
Killing an unarmed man
would suit a coward like you.

965
01:37:57,060 --> 01:37:58,190
Come here.

966
01:37:58,930 --> 01:37:59,980
Come.

967
01:38:10,900 --> 01:38:12,740
Come here.

968
01:38:13,330 --> 01:38:14,420
Come.

969
01:38:15,980 --> 01:38:17,260
You traitor!

970
01:38:17,750 --> 01:38:19,230
Stop!

971
01:38:20,140 --> 01:38:22,610
Leave me be and
I'll tell you everthing.

972
01:38:23,600 --> 01:38:25,050
Of course, you will.

973
01:38:26,320 --> 01:38:29,930
But you will tell everything in
front of Ali Bey and Osman Bey.

974
01:38:32,740 --> 01:38:33,830
Come.

975
01:38:34,130 --> 01:38:36,410
Walk! Come on!

976
01:38:42,160 --> 01:38:43,260
Enough!

977
01:38:44,000 --> 01:38:45,100
Osman Bey.

978
01:38:48,810 --> 01:38:51,760
You talk about justice...

979
01:38:53,000 --> 01:38:55,980
...but slap someone without any evidence.

980
01:38:59,250 --> 01:39:00,370
Ali Bey,...

981
01:39:02,630 --> 01:39:04,250
...you don't believe me, huh?

982
01:39:04,930 --> 01:39:10,210
I see someone who did everything
he could to give Turgut Bey away.

983
01:39:11,790 --> 01:39:13,220
Where is betrayal in that?

984
01:39:14,400 --> 01:39:17,890
The rest is superfluous.

985
01:39:19,960 --> 01:39:21,240
Superfluous?

986
01:39:27,770 --> 01:39:28,770
Come here.

987
01:39:32,010 --> 01:39:33,100
So...

988
01:39:36,620 --> 01:39:37,720
....come here.

989
01:39:37,920 --> 01:39:39,060
If...

990
01:39:39,990 --> 01:39:42,030
...the head is not going to talk...

991
01:39:42,870 --> 01:39:44,630
...then the feet will.

992
01:39:53,210 --> 01:39:54,290
Speak!

993
01:39:59,740 --> 01:40:00,810
Speak!

994
01:40:02,220 --> 01:40:03,830
Barkın was the student of Arius.

995
01:40:03,980 --> 01:40:05,040
Shut up!

996
01:40:05,270 --> 01:40:07,280
He is lying to save his own skin!

997
01:40:16,690 --> 01:40:18,350
They set up everything together.

998
01:40:18,430 --> 01:40:20,210
I have no involvement, my Bey.

999
01:40:20,840 --> 01:40:21,920
I just follow orders.

1000
01:40:22,360 --> 01:40:24,630
Bey told me to do it, so I did it.

1001
01:40:29,950 --> 01:40:31,010
Spare me.

1002
01:40:32,820 --> 01:40:33,860
Forgive me.

1003
01:40:35,620 --> 01:40:36,690
Keep going.

1004
01:40:37,770 --> 01:40:39,120
They blew up Söğüt together.

1005
01:40:41,260 --> 01:40:45,610
Then Umur Bey, and
Ivaz Bey killed all of them.

1006
01:40:57,530 --> 01:40:59,560
Send word to Nikola, Arius...

1007
01:41:00,140 --> 01:41:02,700
...Romanos one by one.

1008
01:41:04,560 --> 01:41:06,720
I told you everything you wanted, my bey.

1009
01:41:08,580 --> 01:41:11,300
Spare my life, I beg of you, my bey!

1010
01:41:17,540 --> 01:41:18,670
Ali Bey,...

1011
01:41:21,030 --> 01:41:22,310
...you're rushing again.

1012
01:41:24,950 --> 01:41:26,310
You got things to hear.

1013
01:41:27,680 --> 01:41:29,210
You got things to see.

1014
01:41:33,690 --> 01:41:34,700
Wait for a bit.

1015
01:41:57,090 --> 01:41:58,160
There.

1016
01:42:03,940 --> 01:42:04,940
You see?

1017
01:42:07,980 --> 01:42:10,090
Do you know who has the same thing?

1018
01:42:20,670 --> 01:42:21,670
Alps!

1019
01:42:23,030 --> 01:42:24,390
Bring him.

1020
01:42:57,920 --> 01:42:58,920
Ali Bey.

1021
01:43:04,350 --> 01:43:05,380
Ata Bey.

1022
01:43:07,040 --> 01:43:08,060
Come here.

1023
01:43:27,330 --> 01:43:29,590
Do you see it?

1024
01:43:31,670 --> 01:43:34,180
That is the evidence of
Ahmet being one of them.

1025
01:43:46,000 --> 01:43:48,810
How could Ahmet...

1026
01:44:14,210 --> 01:44:15,450
You tricked me.

1027
01:44:16,740 --> 01:44:18,540
You made me a part of your treachery.

1028
01:44:20,450 --> 01:44:21,550
Murderers!

1029
01:44:22,510 --> 01:44:24,940
Murderers! Murderers!

1030
01:44:42,540 --> 01:44:44,070
You killed Umur Bey.

1031
01:44:46,470 --> 01:44:49,040
You killed your father-in-law Ivaz Bey.

1032
01:44:50,330 --> 01:44:54,370
You worked with Romanos and Nikola.

1033
01:44:56,380 --> 01:44:58,680
Tell me! Tell me!

1034
01:45:01,190 --> 01:45:02,490
For what?

1035
01:45:07,420 --> 01:45:08,580
People like you...

1036
01:45:10,140 --> 01:45:12,000
...only want the power for themselves.

1037
01:45:13,550 --> 01:45:16,810
Beys, noblesses....

1038
01:45:17,500 --> 01:45:18,720
...nobles...

1039
01:45:20,140 --> 01:45:22,430
...the ones who take posts
from their fathers....

1040
01:45:23,670 --> 01:45:25,200
...ones on the throne...

1041
01:45:32,350 --> 01:45:36,360
...I held on to this life
with my paws, Osman.

1042
01:45:38,990 --> 01:45:40,830
Humans are born alone...

1043
01:45:42,460 --> 01:45:43,600
...die alone.

1044
01:45:45,100 --> 01:45:46,680
I lived alone.

1045
01:45:48,810 --> 01:45:51,760
Now, you may ask: "why?"

1046
01:45:53,500 --> 01:45:55,130
I'll tell you why.

1047
01:45:57,150 --> 01:45:58,360
For power.

1048
01:46:00,060 --> 01:46:01,580
To be acknowledged.

1049
01:46:04,830 --> 01:46:06,430
I was dropped on the sea...

1050
01:46:08,110 --> 01:46:09,720
...and hugged Arius.

1051
01:46:16,270 --> 01:46:17,960
This power is poisonous, Osman.

1052
01:46:20,010 --> 01:46:22,650
I became a Bey and it wasn't enough.

1053
01:46:24,040 --> 01:46:27,740
Everyone close to me is a threat to me.

1054
01:46:28,680 --> 01:46:32,160
I made a deal with the
devil to destroy you.

1055
01:46:37,290 --> 01:46:41,400
I killed Umur.

1056
01:46:42,720 --> 01:46:44,700
And I killed Ivaz as well.

1057
01:46:47,120 --> 01:46:54,960
Also, the one from my
blood Ahmet, I killed him too.

1058
01:47:05,530 --> 01:47:06,750
Ali Bey.

1059
01:47:08,430 --> 01:47:13,040
You were looking for the killer.

1060
01:47:24,240 --> 01:47:26,560
The ones I killed are
waiting for me, Osman.

1061
01:47:26,960 --> 01:47:28,080
Come on.

1062
01:47:29,530 --> 01:47:34,570
But I'm happy that
I'll reunite with Selvi.

1063
01:47:42,800 --> 01:47:43,840
Come on!

1064
01:47:47,040 --> 01:47:52,170
Scoundrels like you don't
deserve a righteous love.

1065
01:47:55,530 --> 01:48:00,620
How could you look at the face
of the Hatun you killed the father of?

1066
01:48:04,650 --> 01:48:09,550
Shame on the ones who sell
their soul and honor for power.

1067
01:48:24,860 --> 01:48:30,010
You came without blood,
you'll leave without blood.

1068
01:48:53,340 --> 01:48:55,310
Your revenge is taken, Mari.

1069
01:49:09,820 --> 01:49:11,660
In the name of Allah the merciful.

1070
01:49:22,080 --> 01:49:23,230
Alaaddin.

1071
01:49:24,060 --> 01:49:25,210
My prince.

1072
01:49:27,560 --> 01:49:31,230
What is it that's making you sad? Tell me.

1073
01:49:35,120 --> 01:49:36,600
I can't, my sheik grandfather.

1074
01:49:37,200 --> 01:49:38,000
I'm embarrassed.

1075
01:49:39,900 --> 01:49:42,170
Why, is it a bad thing?

1076
01:49:42,320 --> 01:49:43,620
I look at my father...

1077
01:49:44,080 --> 01:49:46,350
...he cries on his prayer rug every night.

1078
01:49:47,950 --> 01:49:50,160
Isn't that right brother, you see it too.

1079
01:49:50,830 --> 01:49:54,730
In dawning time and after isha prayer
he cries on his prayer rug reading Quran.

1080
01:49:54,990 --> 01:49:56,640
Every day, every night.

1081
01:49:56,890 --> 01:49:59,870
I asked him once, my sheik grandfather.

1082
01:50:00,140 --> 01:50:01,820
I asked: "Why are you crying?"

1083
01:50:02,480 --> 01:50:03,820
''Because of love'' he said.

1084
01:50:04,680 --> 01:50:08,800
He was crying for his love for Allah
and the prophet.

1085
01:50:10,840 --> 01:50:13,260
So, how is this bad, shehzad?

1086
01:50:13,420 --> 01:50:16,090
The bad is not on my father
but on me.

1087
01:50:16,990 --> 01:50:18,200
I can't cry.

1088
01:50:18,640 --> 01:50:23,070
Don't I love our Allah and prophet?

1089
01:50:23,580 --> 01:50:25,710
I don't know how to increase my love.

1090
01:50:26,330 --> 01:50:29,310
Firstly, know this, children.

1091
01:50:30,320 --> 01:50:34,090
Not everyone is created
the same way.

1092
01:50:35,420 --> 01:50:38,490
Some leak their love out
of their eyes.

1093
01:50:39,160 --> 01:50:44,730
Some give life to a flower, a tree
with their love...

1094
01:50:45,600 --> 01:50:48,400
or mercy to humans.

1095
01:50:51,080 --> 01:50:55,610
Thank Allah, your father does
both of them.

1096
01:50:55,690 --> 01:51:02,350
But don't be sad for not crying.

1097
01:51:03,100 --> 01:51:08,840
Even being sad about this shows
how big your love is.

1098
01:51:09,130 --> 01:51:13,150
You already love but...

1099
01:51:13,770 --> 01:51:22,190
you ask how you can love Allah
and the prophet more!

1100
01:51:23,230 --> 01:51:26,830
The way to that is Marifetullah.

1101
01:51:27,290 --> 01:51:29,640
What is Marifetullah,
my sheik grandfather?

1102
01:51:31,360 --> 01:51:34,140
Marifetullah is science.

1103
01:51:35,720 --> 01:51:38,460
Science of knowing Allah.

1104
01:51:39,720 --> 01:51:44,270
Loving comes after knowing.

1105
01:51:44,640 --> 01:51:55,120
To know Allah, you should know the
prophets and Qur-an.

1106
01:51:55,260 --> 01:52:03,240
Whatever your tongue speaks of,
takes place in your heart.

1107
01:52:03,600 --> 01:52:07,550
For that reason, we praise Allah
five times a day.

1108
01:52:11,800 --> 01:52:17,530
Hz.Muhammad, peace be upon his name,
we say...

1109
01:52:18,220 --> 01:52:24,700
we speak his name and send regards
to him.

1110
01:52:25,500 --> 01:52:28,800
This increases our love.

1111
01:52:29,240 --> 01:52:32,380
The other thing that will
increase our love is...

1112
01:52:32,990 --> 01:52:35,930
learning Prophet Muhammad's sayings.

1113
01:52:36,750 --> 01:52:39,900
What do we say when
we learn it?

1114
01:52:40,460 --> 01:52:45,020
We see how the prophet lived.

1115
01:52:46,650 --> 01:52:55,180
Loving Allah and the prophet is living
Islam and spreading it.

1116
01:52:56,060 --> 01:53:02,560
As sincere and strong
our efforts are...

1117
01:53:03,100 --> 01:53:06,190
our love will increase.

1118
01:53:07,870 --> 01:53:12,320
May your love last forever.

1119
01:53:13,690 --> 01:53:15,050
Amin, my sheik grandfather.

1120
01:53:15,610 --> 01:53:17,020
Amin, my sheik grandfather.

1121
01:53:18,540 --> 01:53:19,560
Amin.

1122
01:53:25,950 --> 01:53:28,300
The horsemen are coming!

1123
01:53:36,840 --> 01:53:38,890
My beautiful wife.

1124
01:53:39,960 --> 01:53:41,960
Allah bless your hands.

1125
01:53:44,000 --> 01:53:45,960
You are still hungry. Here.

1126
01:53:51,180 --> 01:53:52,600
Take it.

1127
01:54:04,670 --> 01:54:06,030
My valiant husband.

1128
01:54:09,310 --> 01:54:11,550
Eat quickly.
We have a job to do.

1129
01:54:11,760 --> 01:54:15,720
You speak so smoothly lately.

1130
01:54:20,990 --> 01:54:22,460
Aren't you mad at me?

1131
01:54:24,350 --> 01:54:25,740
I'm not, Cerkutay.

1132
01:54:25,980 --> 01:54:27,230
Allah Allah!

1133
01:54:30,000 --> 01:54:34,140
Our Mother Selcan's efforts
worked!

1134
01:54:34,280 --> 01:54:35,900
Thank Allah!

1135
01:54:36,270 --> 01:54:38,160
If you don't want smooth...

1136
01:54:38,490 --> 01:54:41,240
I can be harsh too, Cerkutay.

1137
01:54:45,390 --> 01:54:47,290
Thank you, my wife.

1138
01:54:48,680 --> 01:54:50,910
You are the crown of my head.

1139
01:55:06,060 --> 01:55:07,070
Cerkutay.

1140
01:55:11,280 --> 01:55:14,730
If someday...

1141
01:55:16,890 --> 01:55:18,720
something happens to me...

1142
01:55:20,830 --> 01:55:23,340
and I die before you...
-What are you saying, Aygül?

1143
01:55:25,280 --> 01:55:27,290
What are you saying, mad girl?

1144
01:55:30,160 --> 01:55:31,230
Allah forbid.

1145
01:55:31,870 --> 01:55:33,000
Allah forbid.

1146
01:55:33,610 --> 01:55:35,840
Allah forbid.
Of course, Cerkutay.

1147
01:55:38,030 --> 01:55:39,280
But if...

1148
01:55:40,570 --> 01:55:43,040
something like that happens...

1149
01:55:44,480 --> 01:55:46,680
our children are yours to protect.

1150
01:55:50,160 --> 01:55:52,090
Don't let them miss me.

1151
01:55:52,800 --> 01:55:53,950
Don't say that, Aygül!

1152
01:55:54,280 --> 01:55:55,900
Don't say that, mad girl!

1153
01:56:08,940 --> 01:56:10,140
I know you.

1154
01:56:12,400 --> 01:56:15,240
Whenever someone dies,
you are like this.

1155
01:56:19,290 --> 01:56:21,330
Death is real, Cerkutay.

1156
01:56:30,140 --> 01:56:31,600
They are coming.

1157
01:56:31,770 --> 01:56:33,440
Come on, Cerkutay.

1158
01:56:40,140 --> 01:56:42,170
If death will come...

1159
01:56:43,290 --> 01:56:45,210
it should come to me first.

1160
01:56:50,060 --> 01:56:51,160
Come on.

1161
01:56:51,790 --> 01:56:53,390
Let's inform them.

1162
01:57:09,410 --> 01:57:10,640
They are coming.

1163
01:57:10,760 --> 01:57:12,400
Be ready.

1164
01:57:17,840 --> 01:57:20,380
Sisters! Be ready!

1165
01:57:21,200 --> 01:57:23,050
Thank you, Osman Bey.

1166
01:57:24,890 --> 01:57:31,680
As you said then, you woke us up
from our sleep of negligence.

1167
01:57:33,020 --> 01:57:35,680
Thank you. Thank you.

1168
01:57:39,710 --> 01:57:45,820
Kayı's banner will stay in the shadow of
justice to those who want battle.

1169
01:57:47,150 --> 01:57:51,290
Those who have the courage for
their hearts should come with us.

1170
01:57:53,340 --> 01:57:54,080
Thank you.

1171
01:58:14,160 --> 01:58:15,150
Come on!

1172
01:58:52,720 --> 01:58:54,220
Come on, mad girl!

1173
01:58:54,410 --> 01:58:55,820
Come on, sisters!

1174
01:59:01,710 --> 01:59:02,430
Come on!

1175
01:59:14,860 --> 01:59:15,900
Don't be afraid.

1176
01:59:16,360 --> 01:59:18,430
We won't hurt you.

1177
01:59:19,100 --> 01:59:23,020
We won't harm you. We just
want your clothes.

1178
01:59:25,560 --> 01:59:27,040
You'll wear those.

1179
01:59:27,080 --> 01:59:28,510
And we'll wear your
clothes.

1180
01:59:28,760 --> 01:59:30,890
I hope you won't resist.

1181
01:59:32,680 --> 01:59:38,360
Don't be afraid. We'll host you in a
safe place until we are done.

1182
01:59:38,410 --> 01:59:39,610
Women.

1183
01:59:40,700 --> 01:59:42,810
Go and change your clothes
over there.

1184
01:59:42,960 --> 01:59:43,880
Come on.

1185
01:59:58,890 --> 02:00:00,010
Alps.

1186
02:00:01,000 --> 02:00:02,220
Go to Osman Bey.

1187
02:00:02,480 --> 02:00:04,350
Tell him that it's going as planned.

1188
02:00:56,830 --> 02:00:58,250
At the end of the street.

1189
02:00:58,430 --> 02:01:00,670
I saw him with Osman,
Commander Romanos.

1190
02:01:00,670 --> 02:01:02,200
He was in a disguise...

1191
02:01:02,410 --> 02:01:04,820
but I know that it's the same person.

1192
02:01:10,220 --> 02:01:11,430
Call a support unit!

1193
02:01:11,430 --> 02:01:12,680
Right away, sir.

1194
02:01:13,320 --> 02:01:15,250
I won't leave here before
finding them.

1195
02:01:16,690 --> 02:01:18,630
They are galloping toward us.

1196
02:01:18,630 --> 02:01:21,160
But they'll get hit by the
Roman spears!

1197
02:02:15,280 --> 02:02:17,900
It's been a long time, Konur...
...Alp.

1198
02:02:20,020 --> 02:02:21,480
It's true, Uğurlu.

1199
02:02:22,710 --> 02:02:25,500
Seeing you like this broke
my heart, Konur.

1200
02:02:25,840 --> 02:02:28,010
When I left you, you were
with the vizier.

1201
02:02:28,390 --> 02:02:30,840
Now, you are an alp of
a Turkmen bey.

1202
02:02:31,330 --> 02:02:34,410
And I'm the envoy of the Seljuks
in their palace.

1203
02:02:35,890 --> 02:02:39,180
It's an honor to stand behind
Osman Bey who follows justice.

1204
02:02:40,580 --> 02:02:42,730
It's the cause that I
believe in, Uğurlu.

1205
02:02:42,760 --> 02:02:45,040
But you only believe in the palace.

1206
02:02:48,660 --> 02:02:50,390
Welcome, brother Balaban.

1207
02:02:50,620 --> 02:02:52,390
Thank you, brother.

1208
02:02:54,660 --> 02:02:56,770
-I came--
-We don't have much time now.

1209
02:02:59,480 --> 02:03:00,790
You took a long way.

1210
02:03:01,250 --> 02:03:03,640
Let's go to the tribe.
Osman Bey is waiting.

1211
02:03:05,530 --> 02:03:06,260
Alps!

1212
02:03:55,320 --> 02:03:58,420
In the name of God, the infinitely
Compassionate and Merciful.

1213
02:03:59,690 --> 02:04:04,940
Praise be to God, Lord of all the worlds.
The Compassionate, the Merciful. Ruler...

1214
02:04:27,660 --> 02:04:29,410
Come on, we need to go!
Come on!

1215
02:04:29,760 --> 02:04:31,940
What's the situation?
Say it first, smith!

1216
02:04:32,070 --> 02:04:34,070
There is no time, Kumral!
Come on!

1217
02:04:34,410 --> 02:04:37,680
Turn into a priest and lest run
before Romanos' dogs come.

1218
02:04:37,730 --> 02:04:39,600
Go to every street!

1219
02:04:39,600 --> 02:04:41,830
Search every house!

1220
02:04:44,660 --> 02:04:45,900
It's too late now!

1221
02:04:46,290 --> 02:04:47,570
The soldiers are coming!

1222
02:04:56,260 --> 02:04:57,820
Well, Kumral.

1223
02:04:58,220 --> 02:05:01,180
It's time to fight shoulder
to shoulder, huh?

1224
02:05:01,640 --> 02:05:04,000
We've seen this day too.

1225
02:05:06,000 --> 02:05:12,140
We'll leave this street by killing
them one by one.

1226
02:05:14,290 --> 02:05:16,710
Probably, you will all die!

1227
02:05:17,080 --> 02:05:18,340
And even me!

1228
02:05:18,970 --> 02:05:20,560
Why is the happiness?

1229
02:05:21,730 --> 02:05:24,800
Martyrs aren't dead, Priest Hristo.

1230
02:05:25,240 --> 02:05:27,570
Martyrs are always alive.

1231
02:05:30,000 --> 02:05:37,360
-Allah is eternal!
-Allah is righteous!

1232
02:05:38,940 --> 02:05:40,630
Open every door!

1233
02:05:40,890 --> 02:05:42,820
Search every house!

1234
02:05:59,290 --> 02:06:00,090
Beys!

1235
02:06:01,410 --> 02:06:05,710
Before the conquest, we solved
every issue!

1236
02:06:06,390 --> 02:06:08,940
Thank Allah.

1237
02:06:09,490 --> 02:06:10,700
-Boran.
-My bey.

1238
02:06:22,390 --> 02:06:27,940
Here! Here is Umur Bey and İhvaz Bey's
murderer!

1239
02:06:28,910 --> 02:06:32,240
And the head of many other
evil!

1240
02:06:32,910 --> 02:06:34,520
Treacherous Barkın!

1241
02:06:41,180 --> 02:06:43,620
We made him pay!

1242
02:06:47,780 --> 02:06:49,620
Now we found the traitors!

1243
02:06:52,140 --> 02:06:59,110
Now, whoever holds his leashes,
we'll go after them!

1244
02:07:16,150 --> 02:07:18,330
If anyone has an issue, he should say it.

1245
02:07:25,740 --> 02:07:27,750
If you don't have an issue.

1246
02:07:29,820 --> 02:07:33,640
Then, it's time we turn our
face to the West!

1247
02:07:35,790 --> 02:07:38,220
Our alps barely hold their
weapons on their sheaths.

1248
02:07:40,220 --> 02:07:43,660
I see that alps are ready for battle!

1249
02:07:44,240 --> 02:07:48,670
We are ready, my bey!
We are ready, my bey!

1250
02:07:50,130 --> 02:07:54,560
Then, we'll turn our horses
to the West!

1251
02:07:58,000 --> 02:08:00,550
I pity those who'll stand
in our way.

1252
02:08:05,310 --> 02:08:06,860
It's time.

1253
02:09:25,060 --> 02:09:26,100
Let him come.

1254
02:09:35,400 --> 02:09:39,600
My bey, the envoy brought news
from Sultan Alahaddin.

1255
02:09:43,550 --> 02:09:44,730
Speak.

1256
02:09:44,980 --> 02:09:50,850
Osman Bey, my words belong to Seljuk
sultan Alahaddin.

1257
02:09:50,850 --> 02:09:52,790
My words are his words.

1258
02:10:01,440 --> 02:10:04,410
The bey of Kayı, protector
of the borders, Osman Bey.

1259
02:10:04,830 --> 02:10:09,470
I hear that you forget that you are my
shadow. You act on your own.

1260
02:10:10,130 --> 02:10:13,920
Your ears are deaf to my words.
Your tongue knows no respect.

1261
02:10:13,920 --> 02:10:16,900
Now, you want to take Yenişehir.

1262
02:10:17,450 --> 02:10:18,900
I don't allow it.

1263
02:10:19,610 --> 02:10:21,730
If my words are ignored again...

1264
02:10:22,130 --> 02:10:25,660
The army marching from Konya will
crush you.

1265
02:10:25,660 --> 02:10:28,330
This will be my last word to you.

1266
02:10:45,500 --> 02:10:48,140
I heard Sultan Alahaddin's words.

1267
02:10:49,590 --> 02:10:50,710
But...

1268
02:10:54,110 --> 02:10:56,010
but I won't send a messenger.

1269
02:10:57,350 --> 02:11:04,030
You'll personally convey
my words to Sultan Alahaddin.

1270
02:11:06,860 --> 02:11:11,720
Kayı Tribe isn't anyone's shadow!

1271
02:11:13,610 --> 02:11:18,050
Is there are free country in Konya
that we can be the shadow of?

1272
02:11:21,450 --> 02:11:28,360
The Kayı, Kızılbeyoğlu,
and all the tribes on the borders...

1273
02:11:30,000 --> 02:11:32,430
they are all under my rule!

1274
02:11:35,100 --> 02:11:40,290
Now, tell Sultan Alahaddin.
I'm going to take Yenişehir.

1275
02:11:43,250 --> 02:11:50,220
And when I return, I'll have khutbah
read in my name in İnegöl!

1276
02:11:52,220 --> 02:11:54,220
And I'll have my own coins.

1277
02:12:00,780 --> 02:12:03,510
Whoever holds the banner
on the borders...

1278
02:12:07,390 --> 02:12:09,390
holds the rule!

1279
02:13:11,900 --> 02:13:13,050
O' people!

1280
02:13:14,840 --> 02:13:18,890
We'll put Islam's flag
in Yenişehir!

1281
02:13:20,420 --> 02:13:24,460
And Yenişehir will be our home!

1282
02:13:25,030 --> 02:13:31,420
And at the same time, for Bursa and
İznik's conquest, it'll be our quarters.

1283
02:13:32,690 --> 02:13:35,550
Rome's winds are harsh on us.

1284
02:13:36,600 --> 02:13:41,570
But those who can't stand against
those winds are destined to fly away!

1285
02:13:43,520 --> 02:13:46,370
If we can't stand tall gainst
that wind...

1286
02:13:47,290 --> 02:13:51,410
then we'll be removed from these lands.

1287
02:13:53,300 --> 02:13:57,310
For that reason!
O' the people!

1288
02:13:58,050 --> 02:14:00,010
O' the warriors of Kayı!

1289
02:14:01,670 --> 02:14:03,590
For the world's order...

1290
02:14:04,590 --> 02:14:06,680
for Allah's words!

1291
02:14:09,750 --> 02:14:15,580
Our target is Yenişehir!

1292
02:14:17,850 --> 02:14:19,020
Allahu Akbar!

1293
02:14:19,020 --> 02:14:33,900
Allahu Akbar! Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar! Allahu Akbar!

1294
02:14:34,180 --> 02:15:14,380
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com